ading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest#topicname-and-partition-count-parsing","content":"TopicName and partition count parsing"},"3107":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest#validation-of-segmentmode-and-fetchmode","content":"Validation of SegmentMode and FetchMode"},"3108":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest#failure-modes-and-startup-refusal","content":"Failure modes and startup refusal"},"3109":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest#flushpolicy-and-retention-configuration","content":"FlushPolicy and retention configuration"},"3110":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest#key-files","content":"Key files"},"3111":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest#behaviour-that-does-surprise","content":"Behaviour that does surprise"},"3112":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-15, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"3113":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest#booblikconfig-loading-precedence","content":"The configuration follows a strict hierarchy where environment variables take the highest precedence, followed by properties defined in a file, and finally falling back to hardcoded defaults if no value is provided (`BooblikConfig.kt:79-91`). For example, an environment variable like `BOOBLIK_PORT` will override a `booblik.port` setting found in a properties file (`BooblikConfigTest.kt:46-47`)."},"3114":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest#topicname-and-partition-count-parsing","content":"The configuration parses a comma-separated string of topics into a map where each `TopicName` is associated with an integer representing its partition count (`BooblikConfig.kt:144-154`). The format required is `name:partitions` (e.g., `orders:3, clicks:1`), and the parser ensures that each topic has at least one partition (`BooblikConfig.kt:152`)."},"3115":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest#validation-of-segmentmode-and-fetchmode","content":"Enum-based settings are strictly validated against their allowed values during the loading process (`BooblikConfig.kt:106-114`). The following table summarizes the configuration parameters:"},"3116":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest#validation-of-segmentmode-and-fetchmode","content":"Parameter"},"3117":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest#validation-of-segmentmode-and-fetchmode","content":"Type"},"3118":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/booblikconfigtest#validation-of-segmentmode-and-fetchmode","content":"Default / Example"},"3119":{"id":"/