,"page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"Configuration is handled by the `BooblikConfig` data class, which ensures that the broker only boots if all parameters are valid. The loading logic follows a strict precedence: environment variables override properties files, which in turn override default values (`BooblikConfig.kt:77-91`)."},"3176":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"The configuration parameters are parsed as follows:"},"3177":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"Parameter"},"3178":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"Type"},"3179":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"Default / Source"},"3180":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`booblik.data.dir`"},"3181":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`Path`"},"3182":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`\"data\"`"},"3183":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`booblik.port`"},"3184":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`Int`"},"3185":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`9092`"},"3186":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`booblik.topics`"},"3187":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`Map<TopicName, Int>`"},"3188":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`\"default:1\"`"},"3189":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-25","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`booblik.segment.mode`"},"3190":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-26","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`SegmentMode`"},"3191":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-27","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`MAPPED`"},"3192":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-28","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`booblik.transport`"},"3193":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-29","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`Transport`"},"3194":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-30","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`SELECTOR`"},"3195":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-31","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`booblik.fetch.mode`"},"3196":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-32","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`FetchMode`"},"3197":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-33","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"`ZERO_COPY`"},"3198":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-34","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"Validation is performed during initialization to prevent runtime failures (`BooblikConfig.kt:49-55`)."},"3199":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-35","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfig","content":"More: BooblikConfig"},"3200":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-36","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#main-execution-lifecycle","content":"The startup sequence begins in `Main.kt`, where the configuration is loaded and the `Broker` and `BooblikServer` are initialized (`Main.kt:34-73`). Once the server starts listening, the main thread enters a waiting state using a `CountDownLatch` (`Main.kt:90-103`)."},"3201":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-37","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#main-execution-lifecycle","content":"A shutdown hook is registered to ensure a graceful exit: it closes the server first, then cancels background coroutines, and finally closes the broker to ensure all data batches reach the disk (`Main.kt:92-98`)."},"3202":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-38","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#main-execution-lifecycle","content":"More: Main execution lifecycle"},"3203":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-39","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#metrics-reporting-and-retention","content":"The application launches two primary background coroutines using a `SupervisorJob` to manage long-running tasks (`Main.kt:84-86`)."},"3204":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-40","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#metrics-reporting-and-retention","content":"**Metrics Reporting**: The `reportMetrics` function calculates rates by comparing snapshots of the `Metrics` object over a specified interval (`Main.kt:113-125`)."},"3205":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-41","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#metrics-reporting-and-retention","content":"**Retention Policy**: The `applyRetention` function periodically triggers the broker to remove segments based on configured time or size limits (`Main.kt:135-144`)."},"3206":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-42","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#metrics-reporting-and-retention","content":"More: Metrics reporting and retention"},"3207":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-43","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#health-check-mechanism","content":"The `Health` object provides a standalone utility to verify that the broker is not just accepting TCP connections, but is actually capable of processing requests (`Health.kt:20-21`). It performs a `METADATA` request via a `BooblikClient`."},"3208":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-44","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#health-check-mechanism","content":"To prevent the health check from hanging if the broker is unresponsive, the check uses a worker thread with a join timeout (`Health.kt:66-73`). A successful check requires a `MetadataResult` with an `ErrorCode.NONE` (`Health.kt:81-84`)."},"3209":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-45","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#build-and-distribution","content":"The module is configured via `build.gradle.kts` as a Kotlin JVM application (`build.gradle.kts:1-11`). It uses the `application` plugin to define the main entry point and customizes the distribution to include a specific health check script (`build.gradle.kts:29-46`)."},"3210":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-46","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#build-and-distribution","content":"The application's runtime behavior is influenced by JVM arguments, which are explicitly printed at startup to ensure the running profile matches the intended one (`Main.kt:44-45`)."},"3211":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-47","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"File"},"3212":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-48","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3213":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-49","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3214":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-50","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`booblik-app/build.gradle.kts`"},"3215":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-51","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`13-19`"},"3216":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-52","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"Application main class and JVM argument configuration"},"3217":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-53","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`…/app/BooblikConfig.kt`"},"3218":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-54","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`32-48`"},"3219":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-55","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"Data class definition and configuration properties"},"3220":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-56","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`…/app/Health.kt`"},"3221":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-57","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`32-86`"},"3222":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-58","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"Health check logic and client interaction"},"3223":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-59","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`…/app/Main.kt`"},"3224":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-60","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`33-104`"},"3225":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-61","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"Main entry point and shutdown hook implementation"},"3226":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-62","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"`BooblikConfig.load` will throw an exception if a configuration file is explicitly provided but cannot be found, rather than silently using defaults (`BooblikConfig.kt:82-86`)."},"3227":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-63","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"The `Health` check uses a separate thread to bound the request time, because a blocking read on a `SocketChannel` does not respond to `SO_TIMEOUT` (`Health.kt:47-49`)."},"3228":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-64","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"`Main.kt` uses a `CountDownLatch` to keep the main thread alive, ensuring the process doesn't exit until the shutdown hook completes (`Main.kt:90-103`)."},"3229":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","type":"page","content":"Main execution lifecycle","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-app"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle"},"3230":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"3231":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#booblikserver-startup-and-transport-selection","content":"BooblikServer startup and transport selection"},"3232":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#the-acceptor-loop-and-connection-handling","content":"The acceptor loop and connection handling"},"3233":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#session-lifecycle-and-fetchmode-execution","content":"Session lifecycle and FetchMode execution"},"3234":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#graceful-shutdown-and-the-order-of-closure","content":"Graceful shutdown and the order of closure"},"3235":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#smoke-tests-and-distribution-verification","content":"Smoke tests and distribution verification"},"3236":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#key-files","content":"Key files"},"3237":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"Behaviour that surprising"},"3238":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `ef58254ca7be`, 2026-08-16, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"3239":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#booblikserver-startup-and-transport-selection","content":"The server initialization begins by binding a `ServerSocketChannel` to the configured address and port `BooblikServer.kt:134-140`. Once bound, the server selects a transport mechanism based on the `Transport` enum `BooblikServer.kt:25-34`:"},"3240":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#booblikserver-startup-and-transport-selection","content":"Transport"},"3241":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#booblikserver-startup-and-transport-selection","content":"Description"},"3242":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#booblikserver-startup-and-transport-selection","content":"`SELECTOR`"},"3243":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#booblikserver-startup-and-transport-selection","content":"Uses a dedicated selector loop with one coroutine per connection."},"3244":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#booblikserver-startup-and-transport-selection","content":"`VIRTUAL_THREADS`"},"3245":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#booblikserver-startup-and-transport-selection","content":"Uses blocking sockets with one virtual thread per connection."},"3246":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#the-acceptor-loop-and-connection-handling","content":"The acceptor mechanism differs by transport. In `SELECTOR` mode, a coroutine runs a loop that calls `serverChannel.accept()` `BooblikServer.kt:164-175`, where transient exceptions are caught and logged to metrics to prevent the loop from dying. In `VIRTUAL_THREADS` mode, a platform thread runs the acceptor loop `BooblikServer.kt:204-224`. To ensure that a single failing client session does not crash the entire server, `BooblikServer` uses a `SupervisorJob` `BooblikServer.kt:123`, which isolates failures to the specific coroutine scope of that session."},"3247":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#session-lifecycle-and-fetchmode-execution","content":"A `Session` is established when a connection is accepted and configured `BooblikServer.kt:182`. The `FetchMode` determines how data is transferred from the log to the client `BooblikServer.kt:37-43`:"},"3248":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#session-lifecycle-and-fetchmode-execution","content":"FetchMode"},"3249":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#session-lifecycle-and-fetchmode-execution","content":"Mechanism"},"3250":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#session-lifecycle-and-fetchmode-execution","content":"`ZERO_COPY`"},"3251":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#session-lifecycle-and-fetchmode-execution","content":"Uses `transferTo` to move data from the page cache directly to the socket."},"3252":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#session-lifecycle-and-fetchmode-execution","content":"`HEAP`"},"3253":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#session-lifecycle-and-fetchmode-execution","content":"Reads data into a heap buffer before writing."},"3254":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#graceful-shutdown-and-the-order-of-closure","content":"The shutdown process is triggered by a JVM shutdown hook that ensures a specific sequence of closure to prevent data loss `Main.kt:91-100`. The order is strictly:"},"3255":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-25","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#graceful-shutdown-and-the-order-of-closure","content":"`server.close()` to stop accepting new connections."},"3256":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-26","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#graceful-shutdown-and-the-order-of-closure","content":"`background.cancel()` to stop background tasks like retention."},"3257":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-27","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#graceful-shutdown-and-the-order-of-closure","content":"`broker.close()` to ensure all writers finish flushing batches to disk before the underlying log is closed."},"3258":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-28","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#smoke-tests-and-distribution-verification","content":"The `ci/smoke.sh` script performs a full end-to-end verification of the distribution `smoke.sh:30-34`. It builds the `installDist` distribution, starts the broker, and uses a Python script to perform `PRODUCE` and `FETCH` operations over the wire. This verifies that the broker can recover its state from disk after a restart `smoke.sh:130-142` and that the wire format (including CRC32C checksums) is correctly implemented."},"3259":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-29","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#key-files","content":"File"},"3260":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-30","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3261":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-31","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3262":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-32","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#key-files","content":"`…/app/Main.kt`"},"3263":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-33","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#key-files","content":"`33-104`"},"3264":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-34","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#key-files","content":"The main entry point, orchestration of server/broker, and shutdown hooks."},"3265":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-35","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#key-files","content":"`…/net/BooblikServer.kt`"},"3266":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-36","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#key-files","content":"`117-260`"},"3267":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-37","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#key-files","content":"The network server implementation, transport selection, and session management."},"3268":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-38","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#key-files","content":"`ci/smoke.sh`"},"3269":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-39","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#key-files","content":"`30-144`"},"3270":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-40","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#key-files","content":"The smoke test script for distribution and protocol verification."},"3271":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-41","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"The `BooblikServer` uses a `SupervisorJob` `BooblikServer.kt:123` specifically so that a client sending \"nonsense\" only kills its own session and not the entire server."},"3272":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-42","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"The `applyRetention` function `Main.kt:135` is the only place that decides *when* retention happens, as the `Broker` itself has no internal clock."},"3273":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle-43","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/main-execution-lifecycle#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"The `booblik.metrics.interval.millis` setting `Main.kt:118` allows disabling metrics by setting it to `0`, which results in silent operation rather than an error."},"3274":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","type":"page","content":"Metrics reporting and retention","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-app"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and"},"3275":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"3276":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#metrics-snapshotting-and-rate-reporting","content":"Metrics snapshotting and rate reporting"},"3277":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#the-applyretention-timer","content":"The `applyRetention` timer"},"3278":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#retention-by-size-and-age","content":"Retention by size and age"},"3279":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#shutdown-sequence-and-data-integrity","content":"Shutdown sequence and data integrity"},"3280":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#key-files","content":"Key files"},"3281":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"Behaviour that surprises"},"3282":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `ef58254ca7be`, 2026-08-16, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"3283":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#metrics-snapshotting-and-rate-reporting","content":"The `Metrics` class provides a snapshot of the current state of the `Broker`, which is used to calculate performance. Instead of printing cumulative counters—which would require the operator to perform manual differentiation during an incident—the `reportMetrics` function transforms these raw values into rates (e.g., records per second) by comparing the current snapshot against a previous one over a specific time interval `Main.kt:119-123`. This interval is configurable via `metricsIntervalMillis` in the `BooblikConfig` `BooblikConfig.kt:47`."},"3284":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#the-applyretention-timer","content":"The broker itself is designed to be stateless regarding time, allowing tests to advance time manually by calling `broker.applyRetention` directly `Main.kt:131-133`. The actual temporal logic is encapsulated in a dedicated background coroutine launched in `Main.kt:86` `Main.kt:86`. This loop uses `delay(config.retentionCheckMillis)` to determine when to trigger the retention logic `Main.kt:141`, ensuring that the \"when\" is decoupled from the \"how\" of the broker's internal logic `Main.kt:136-144`."},"3285":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#retention-by-size-and-age","content":"Retention is governed by two optional parameters defined in `BooblikConfig` `BooblikConfig.kt:42-43`:"},"3286":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#retention-by-size-and-age","content":"Key"},"3287":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#retention-by-size-and-age","content":"Type"},"3288":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#retention-by-size-and-age","content":"Description"},"3289":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#retention-by-size-and-age","content":"`retentionBytes`"},"3290":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#retention-by-size-and-age","content":"`Long?`"},"3291":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#retention-by-size-and-age","content":"Maximum total size of the log to keep per partition"},"3292":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#retention-by-size-and-age","content":"`retentionMillis`"},"3293":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#retention-by-size-and-age","content":"`Long?`"},"3294":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#retention-by-size-and-age","content":"Maximum age of a segment to keep"},"3295":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#retention-by-size-and-age","content":"When `applyRetention` is called, the broker removes segments that exceed these thresholds `Main.kt:142`."},"3296":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#shutdown-sequence-and-data-integrity","content":"To prevent data loss, the application follows a strict, layered shutdown sequence within the `Runtime` shutdown hook `Main.kt:91-103`. The order is critical:"},"3297":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#shutdown-sequence-and-data-integrity","content":"The `BooblikServer` is closed first `Main.kt:94`."},"3298":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#shutdown-sequence-and-data-integrity","content":"Background coroutines (metrics and retention) are cancelled via `background.cancel()` to stop any pending tasks `Main.kt:95`."},"3299":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#shutdown-sequence-and-data-integrity","content":"The `broker` is closed last `Main.kt:98`. This ensures that the broker's writers are still active while the server is shutting down, allowing any accepted batches to reach the disk before the underlying log is closed `Main.kt:97-98`."},"3300":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-25","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#key-files","content":"File"},"3301":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-26","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3302":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-27","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3303":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-28","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#key-files","content":"`…/app/Main.kt`"},"3304":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-29","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#key-files","content":"`84-104`"},"3305":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-30","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#key-files","content":"The main loop, shutdown hook, and background coroutine orchestration."},"3306":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-31","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#key-files","content":"`…/app/BooblikConfig.kt`"},"3307":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-32","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#key-files","content":"`42-43`"},"3308":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-33","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#key-files","content":"Configuration properties for retention and metrics intervals."},"3309":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-34","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**Decoupled Time**: The `Broker` does not have its own clock; it relies on an external caller (like the `applyRetention` loop in `Main.kt`) to tell it when to perform maintenance `Main.kt:131-133`."},"3310":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-35","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**Shutdown Order**: The `broker` is closed *after* the background coroutines are cancelled to ensure that any data currently being processed by the server can be flushed to the log before the log itself is closed `Main.kt:95-98`."},"3311":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and-36","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app/metrics-reporting-and#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**Rate-based Metrics**: `reportMetrics` specifically avoids printing cumulative counters to prevent the need for manual differentiation during incident response `Main.kt:110-111`."},"3312":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"page","content":"BooblikClient","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-client"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient"},"3313":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"3314":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#booblikclient","content":"BooblikClient"},"3315":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#pipelined-requests-and-correlation-ids","content":"Pipelined Requests and Correlation IDs"},"3316":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#booblikconnection","content":"BooblikConnection"},"3317":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#ackpolicy-and-response-behavior","content":"AckPolicy and Response Behavior"},"3318":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#fetch-long-polling-and-maxwaitmillis","content":"Fetch Long-Polling and maxWaitMillis"},"3319":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#conformance-testing-scenarios","content":"Conformance Testing Scenarios"},"3320":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"Key files"},"3321":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"Behaviour that surprise"},"3322":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `ef58254ca7be`, 2026-08-16, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"3323":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#booblikclient","content":"The low-level, blocking, single-socket client interface. `BooblikClient` acts as a thin wrapper around a `SocketChannel`, providing synchronous methods to send metadata, produce records, and fetch data `BooblikClient.kt:24-88`. It is designed to be \"dumb\"—it performs no bookkeeping or request queuing itself, leaving that responsibility to higher-level abstractions."},"3324":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#pipelined-requests-and-correlation-ids","content":"Because the broker is guaranteed to answer requests in the exact order they were received, the client can support pipelining. Each request is assigned a unique `correlationId` via an `AtomicInteger` `BooblikConnection.kt:71`. When a response arrives, the client uses a `ConcurrentLinkedQueue` of `Pending` objects to match the response back to the original caller `BooblikConnection.kt:60-70`. If the broker responds out of order, the client detects the mismatch and fails loudly to prevent delivering data to the wrong caller `BooblikConnection.kt:192-195`."},"3325":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#booblikconnection","content":"The coroutine-based implementation of a pipelined connection. It manages two long-running jobs: a `writer` that drains an `outbound` channel to the socket and a `reader` that continuously parses incoming frames `BooblikConnection.kt:74-100`. This architecture ensures that multiple coroutines can concurrently call `produce` or `fetch` without interleaving bytes on the wire, as all writes are serialized through a single coroutine `BooblikConnection.kt:40-47`."},"3326":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#ackpolicy-and-response-behavior","content":"The `AckPolicy` determines whether a producer waits for a response from the broker `BooblikClient.kt:44`."},"3327":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#ackpolicy-and-response-behavior","content":"Policy"},"3328":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#ackpolicy-and-response-behavior","content":"Behavior"},"3329":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#ackpolicy-and-response-behavior","content":"`NONE`"},"3330":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#ackpolicy-and-response-behavior","content":"The request is sent, but no response is expected; the client returns `null` immediately `BooblikClient.kt:48`."},"3331":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#ackpolicy-and-response-behavior","content":"`WRITTEN`"},"3332":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#ackpolicy-and-response-behavior","content":"The client waits for a `ProduceResult` from the broker `BooblikClient.kt:48`."},"3333":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#ackpolicy-and-response-behavior","content":"`FORCED`"},"3334":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#ackpolicy-and-response-behavior","content":"The client waits for the broker to acknowledge the write (implementation details handled by the broker)."},"3335":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#fetch-long-polling-and-maxwaitmillis","content":"The `fetch` request supports long-polling via the `maxWaitMillis` parameter `BooblikClient.kt:57`. If the broker has no data, it can \"hold\" the request for up to the specified duration. While a request is held, it occupies the connection, meaning subsequent requests on that same connection are blocked `LongFetchTest.kt:117-118`. A record arriving at the broker during this wait period will wake the fetch immediately `LongFetchTest.kt:52-70`."},"3336":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#conformance-testing-scenarios","content":"The conformance client verifies the protocol implementation against specific requirements `Main.kt:37-80`. Key checks include:"},"3337":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#conformance-testing-scenarios","content":"**Keyed Production**: Using `Partitioner.Fnv1a` to select a partition based on a key before sending the produce request `Main.kt:158`."},"3338":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-25","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#conformance-testing-scenarios","content":"**Error Reporting**: Ensuring that `CORRUPT_REQUEST` errors (such as `minBytes` being larger than `maxBytes`) are correctly propagated to the client `Main.kt:182`."},"3339":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-26","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"File"},"3340":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-27","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3341":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-28","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3342":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-29","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"`…/client/BooblikClient.kt`"},"3343":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-30","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"`24-88`"},"3344":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-31","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"The low-level blocking client implementation."},"3345":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-32","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"`…/client/BooblikConnection.kt`"},"3346":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-33","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"`50-241`"},"3347":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-34","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"The pipelined, coroutine-based connection logic."},"3348":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-35","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"`…/conformance/Main.kt`"},"3349":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-36","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"`37-80`"},"3350":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-37","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"The reference implementation for conformance testing."},"3351":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-38","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"A held fetch request on a `BooblikConnection` blocks all subsequent requests on that same connection, but does not block requests sent from a different connection `LongFetchTest.kt:97-118`."},"3352":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-39","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"If a `fetch` request is cancelled via a timeout, the abandoned read remains on the socket and may consume the response intended for the next read `LongFetchTest.kt:37-41`."},"3353":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","type":"page","content":"BooblikConnection","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-client"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection"},"3354":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"What this module is responsible for"},"3355":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"3356":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#pipelined-request-response-matching","content":"Pipelined Request-Response Matching"},"3357":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#the-outbound-writer-coroutine","content":"The Outbound Writer Coroutine"},"3358":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#ackpolicynone-and-fire-and-forget-semantics","content":"AckPolicy.NONE and Fire-and-Forget Semantics"},"3359":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#connectionclosedexception-and-failure-propagation","content":"ConnectionClosedException and Failure Propagation"},"3360":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#correlation-id-atomicity","content":"Correlation ID Atomicity"},"3361":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#key-files","content":"Key files"},"3362":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"Behaviour that surprise"},"3363":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `ef58254ca7be`, 2026-08-16, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"3364":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"The `BooblikConnection` class is responsible for managing a single TCP connection to a Booblik broker. It implements a pipelined communication protocol where multiple requests can be in flight simultaneously. It handles the encoding of requests, the asynchronous reading of responses, and the complex task of matching those responses back to the specific coroutines that requested them, all while maintaining strict FIFO ordering guarantees."},"3365":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#pipelined-request-response-matching","content":"Because the broker is guaranteed to answer requests in the exact order they were received, the client uses a FIFO queue to manage pending responses. When a request is sent, a `Pending` object is added to a `ConcurrentLinkedQueue` (as seen in `BooblikConnection.kt:60`). When a response arrives, the `reader` coroutine polls the head of this queue and validates that the `correlationId` in the response matches the expected ID via `checkOrder` (as seen in `BooblikConnection.kt:193`). If the IDs do not match, it indicates the broker has violated the protocol, and the client fails loudly."},"3366":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#the-outbound-writer-coroutine","content":"To prevent interleaved writes where bytes from two different requests might mix on the wire, `BooblikConnection` uses a single-writer pattern. All callers send their requests to an `outbound` `Channel` (as seen in `BooblikConnection.kt:59`), and a single dedicated `writer` coroutine drains this channel to perform the actual socket writes (as seen in `BooblikConnection.kt:73`). This ensures that the order in which requests are enqueued in the channel is exactly the order in which they are written to the `SocketChannel`."},"3367":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#ackpolicynone-and-fire-and-forget-semantics","content":"The client supports a \"fire-and-forget\" mode through the `AckPolicy.NONE` setting. When a request is produced with this policy, the `produce` function skips the creation of a `CompletableDeferred` and does not add anything to the `pending` queue (as seen in `BooblikConnection.kt:110`). The request is simply sent to the `outbound` channel, and the function returns `null` immediately, bypassing the response matching logic entirely."},"3368":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#connectionclosedexception-and-failure-propagation","content":"When a connection fails or is closed, the client must ensure that no caller is left hanging forever. The `fail` function handles this by catching the error and iterating through the `pending` queue to fail every waiting request with a `ConnectionClosedException` (as seen in `BooblikConnection.kt:166`). This ensures that all suspended `await()` calls in the calling coroutines are resumed with an exception, maintaining the integrity of the asynchronous flow."},"3369":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#correlation-id-atomicity","content":"To support high concurrency, `BooblikConnection` uses an `AtomicInteger` to generate `correlationIds` (as seen in `BooblikConnection.kt:71`). This is critical because multiple coroutines call `produce`, `metadata`, or `fetch` concurrently. Using `getAndIncrement()` ensures that every single request receives a unique, monotonically increasing ID, preventing the catastrophic failure where two different callers receive each other's responses (as noted in the documentation at `BooblikConnection.kt:67`)."},"3370":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#key-files","content":"File"},"3371":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3372":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3373":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#key-files","content":"`…/client/BooblikConnection.kt`"},"3374":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#key-files","content":"`50-241`"},"3375":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#key-files","content":"The implementation of the pipelined connection, including the writer/reader coroutines and request matching logic."},"3376":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"**Strict Ordering Requirement**: If the broker sends a response out of order, the client will throw an error rather than attempting to find the correct caller, because the protocol's FIFO guarantee is a prerequisite for correctness (as seen in `BooblikConnection.kt:34`)."},"3377":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"**Blocking the Pipeline**: A single `fetch` request with a long `maxWaitMillis` will block all subsequent requests on the same connection, including `produce` requests, because the connection is served strictly one request at a time (as seen in `BooblikConnection.kt:132`)."},"3378":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikconnection#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"**Silent Failures in Acceptor**: In the server implementation, if the acceptor loop encounters an exception, it is treated as transient to prevent the broker from entering a state where it accepts TCP connections but never processes them (as seen in `BooblikServer.kt:169`)."},"3379":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"page","content":"booblik-client","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-client"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client"},"3380":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"3381":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#booblikclient","content":"BooblikClient"},"3382":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#booblikconnection","content":"BooblikConnection"},"3383":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#producer","content":"Producer"},"3384":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#consumer","content":"Consumer"},"3385":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#responsereader","content":"ResponseReader"},"3386":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#responseencoder","content":"ResponseEncoder"},"3387":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"Key files"},"3388":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"Public API"},"3389":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"Behaviour that surprises"},"3390":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `ef58254ca7be`, 2026-08-16, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"3391":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#booblikclient","content":"The low-level, blocking, single-socket client for sending raw requests. It provides the most basic interface for sending `PRODUCE`, `FETCH`, and `METADATA` requests directly to a `SocketChannel` `BooblikClient.kt:24-88`."},"3392":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#booblikclient","content":"More: BooblikClient"},"3393":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#booblikconnection","content":"The pipelined connection mechanism that manages concurrent requests via a single writer coroutine and a FIFO response queue. It uses an `AtomicInteger` to manage `correlationId`s `BooblikConnection.kt:71` and ensures that responses are matched to callers in strict order, failing loudly if the broker reorders them `BooblikConnection.kt:34-38`."},"3394":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#booblikconnection","content":"More: BooblikConnection"},"3395":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#producer","content":"The high-level accumulator that batches records by partition and manages the `lingerMillis` and `maxBatchSize` logic `Producer.kt:21-34`. It uses a `mailbox` to receive `Command.Append` requests and an internal `runLoop` to decide when to trigger a `deliver` call based on the configured `ProducerConfig` `Producer.kt:54-173`."},"3396":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#producer","content":"More: Producer"},"3397":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#consumer","content":"The stateful reader that manages the `position` offset and handles `RecordExceedsMaxBytesException` during polling `Consumer.kt:56-97`. It tracks the current `position` and advances it only past whole records when a `poll` is successful `Consumer.kt:56-97`."},"3398":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#responsereader","content":"The decoding layer that handles frame reading and checksum verification for FETCH responses. It reads the length-prefixed frames from a `SocketChannel` and delegates decoding to the protocol module, specifically handling the translation of `CorruptRecordException` `ResponseReader.kt:55-109`."},"3399":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#responseencoder","content":"The construction of response frames, specifically the zero-copy header mechanism for FETCH responses. It distinguishes between \"promised\" bytes (the body to be streamed) and \"inline\" bytes (the header) to support efficient zero-copy reading `ResponseEncoder.kt:15-117`."},"3400":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"File"},"3401":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3402":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3403":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"`…/client/BooblikClient.kt`"},"3404":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"`24-88`"},"3405":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-25","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"The low-level blocking client implementation."},"3406":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-26","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"`…/client/BooblikConnection.kt`"},"3407":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-27","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"`50-241`"},"3408":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-28","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"The pipelined connection and coroutine-based writer/reader."},"3409":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-29","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"`…/client/Producer.kt`"},"3410":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-30","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"`54-264`"},"3411":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-31","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files",