ises","content":"`LogSegment.acquire` may return `false` if the segment was retired while the caller was attempting to acquire it, requiring a retry `LogSegment.kt:195`."},"3731":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-75","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"`PartitionLog.transferTo` is designed to never cross a segment boundary because it uses a single file descriptor for the operation `PartitionLog.kt:163`."},"3732":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","type":"page","content":"LogSegment","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-core"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment"},"3733":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"What this module is responsible for"},"3734":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"3735":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#logsegment-architecture","content":"LogSegment Architecture"},"3736":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#segmentmode-file_channel-vs-mapped","content":"SegmentMode: FILE_CHANNEL vs MAPPED"},"3737":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#sparseoffsetindex-mechanics","content":"SparseOffsetIndex Mechanics"},"3738":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#recovery-after-a-crash","content":"Recovery after a crash"},"3739":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#reader-lifecycle-and-concurrency","content":"Reader Lifecycle and Concurrency"},"3740":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#zero-copy-and-heap-based-reading","content":"Zero-copy and Heap-based Reading"},"3741":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#key-files","content":"Key files"},"3742":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"Behaviour that surprise"},"3743":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `ef58254ca7be`, 2026-08-16, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"3744":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","content":"This documentation describes the `LogSegment` component within the `booblik-core` module."},"3745":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"The `LogSegment` is the fundamental unit of storage in the `booblik` log, representing an append-only data file paired with a sparse index. It manages the lifecycle of data on disk, ensuring that records are written with integrity, can be recovered after a crash, and can be read efficiently via both zero-copy and heap-based paths."},"3746":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#logsegment-architecture","content":"A `LogSegment` acts as a coordinator for three primary components: a `SegmentWriter` for appending data, a `FileChannel` for reading, and a `SparseOffsetIndex` for locating records. The architecture is designed to separate read and write concerns; the writer is owned by a single coroutine, while readers run concurrently without locks, relying on the fact that the file is append-only and the `nextOffset` is published only after bytes are written (`LogSegment.kt:30-34`)."},"3747":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#segmentmode-file_channel-vs-mapped","content":"The segment supports two distinct write paths, which differ in how they handle file sizing and the end-of-log sentinel:"},"3748":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#segmentmode-file_channel-vs-mapped","content":"Mode"},"3749":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#segmentmode-file_channel-vs-mapped","content":"File Sizing"},"3750":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#segmentmode-file_channel-vs-mapped","content":"End-of-Log Sentinel"},"3751":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#segmentmode-file_channel-vs-mapped","content":"`FILE_CHANNEL`"},"3752":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#segmentmode-file_channel-vs-mapped","content":"The file length is determined by the actual data written (`LogSegment.kt:287`)"},"3753":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#segmentmode-file_channel-vs-mapped","content":"The file length itself acts as the boundary"},"3754":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#segmentmode-file_channel-vs-mapped","content":"`MAPPED`"},"3755":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#segmentmode-file_channel-vs-mapped","content":"The file is pre-sized to its full `capacity` (`LogSegment.kt:288`)"},"3756":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#segmentmode-file_channel-vs-mapped","content":"A zero-length prefix marks the end of the log"},"3757":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#sparseoffsetindex-mechanics","content":"To avoid the overhead of a full index, the `SparseOffsetIndex` uses intervals to store entries. When a `positionOf(offset)` is called, the index provides the greatest entry at or below the target, and the system performs a forward scan over length prefixes to find the exact position (`LogSegment.kt:96-108`). This mechanism is designed to handle large `baseOffset` values without truncation by storing offsets relative to the base (`SparseOffsetIndexTest.kt:52-57`)."},"3758":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-25","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#recovery-after-a-crash","content":"During startup, the `recover` function reconstructs the index by walking the record headers from the start of the segment (`LogSegment.kt:321-330`). The recovery logic is robust against crashes: it discards \"torn\" records where a length prefix claims more bytes than are available or where the checksum does not match the stored value (`LogSegment.kt:354-365`). In `MAPPED` mode, a crash that leaves an orphaned body without a header is treated as the end of the log (`RecoveryTest.kt:97-101`)."},"3759":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-26","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#reader-lifecycle-and-concurrency","content":"Concurrency is managed through a registration pattern to ensure segments are not closed while readers are active. A reader must call `acquire()` to register itself, which increments an `AtomicInteger` (`LogSegment.kt:195-196`). When a segment is `retire()`-ed, it is unlinked from the file system, but the file descriptor remains open until the last reader calls `release()`, at which point `closeNow()` is invoked (`LogSegment.kt:209-210`)."},"3760":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-27","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#zero-copy-and-heap-based-reading","content":"The segment provides two distinct reading paths:"},"3761":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-28","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#zero-copy-and-heap-based-reading","content":"**Zero-copy:** The `transferTo` method uses `FileChannel.transferTo` to stream bytes directly to a `WritableByteChannel` (like a socket) without touching the JVM heap (`LogSegment.kt:158-166`)."},"3762":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-29","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#zero-copy-and-heap-based-reading","content":"**Heap-based:** The `read(offset)` method allocates a `ByteArray` and performs a manual checksum verification to ensure data integrity (`LogSegment.kt:130-131`)."},"3763":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-30","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#key-files","content":"File"},"3764":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-31","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3765":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-32","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3766":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-33","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#key-files","content":"`…/storage/LogSegment.kt`"},"3767":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-34","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#key-files","content":"`41-48`"},"3768":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-35","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#key-files","content":"The `LogSegment` class definition and its primary properties."},"3769":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-36","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#key-files","content":"`…/storage/LogSegment.kt`"},"3770":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-37","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#key-files","content":"`261-270`"},"3771":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-38","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#key-files","content":"The `open` companion function for initializing and recovering a segment."},"3772":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-39","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#key-files","content":"`…/storage/LogSegment.kt`"},"3773":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-40","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#key-files","content":"`321-343`"},"3774":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-41","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#key-files","content":"The `recover` function implementation for rebuilding the index."},"3775":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-42","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"`LogSegment.open` in `MAPPED` mode results in a file that appears to be its full `capacity` in terms of disk usage/file size, even if it only contains one small record (`ModeMigrationTest.kt:76-85`)."},"3776":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-43","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"`LogSegment.transferTo` is allowed to return fewer bytes than requested, meaning the caller must loop until the entire transfer is complete (`LogSegment.kt:154-156`)."},"3777":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment-44","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/logsegment#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"The `nextOffset` is updated **after** the index and writer have been updated, ensuring that an offset is only visible to readers once its corresponding bytes are safely written (`LogSegment.kt:77-78`)."},"3778":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","type":"page","content":"PartitionLog","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-core"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog"},"3779":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"What this module is responsible for"},"3780":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"3781":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#partitionlog-mechanics","content":"PartitionLog mechanics"},"3782":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#logsegment-lifecycle-and-retention","content":"LogSegment lifecycle and retention"},"3783":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#segmentmode-and-zero-copy-transfer","content":"SegmentMode and zero-copy transfer"},"3784":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#data-integrity-and-recovery-properties","content":"Data integrity and recovery properties"},"3785":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#partitionlog-boundary-and-error-invariants","content":"PartitionLog boundary and error invariants"},"3786":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"Key files"},"3787":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"Behaviour that surprising"},"3788":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `ef58254ca7be`, 2026-08-16, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"3789":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"`PartitionLog` is the core storage component of the `booblik` system, responsible for managing an ordered sequence of `LogSegment` objects. It provides an append-only log abstraction where data is partitioned into segments to facilitate efficient retention (deletion of old data) and high-performance reads."},"3790":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#partitionlog-mechanics","content":"The `PartitionLog` architecture is built on a single-writer, multi-reader concurrency model. To avoid the overhead of locks on the hot path, the segment list is maintained as an immutable `List` behind a `@Volatile` field, which is replaced rather than mutated whenever the log structure changes (e.g., during a `roll` or retention) `PartitionLog.kt:41-42`. This ensures that readers always see a consistent snapshot of the log, either before or after a change, but never a partially mutated list `PartitionLog.kt:19-22`."},"3791":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#logsegment-lifecycle-and-retention","content":"Segments follow a strict lifecycle to ensure data is not deleted while being actively read. Readers must use `acquire()` to claim a segment, which prevents the retention process from closing the segment's descriptors until the reader calls `release()` `PartitionLog.kt:111-116`."},"3792":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#logsegment-lifecycle-and-retention","content":"Retention is performed at the segment level via `retainAtMost` or `retainNewerThan`, which unlinks files from the filesystem to reclaim space `PartitionLog.kt:185-195`. A key safety mechanism is that a segment is removed from the volatile `segments` list *before* `retire()` is called, ensuring new readers cannot find it, while existing readers can continue streaming data from the unlinked file until they release their handle `PartitionLog.kt:27-31`."},"3793":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#segmentmode-and-zero-copy-transfer","content":"The log supports different modes for data persistence and access:"},"3794":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#segmentmode-and-zero-copy-transfer","content":"Mode"},"3795":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#segmentmode-and-zero-copy-transfer","content":"Description"},"3796":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#segmentmode-and-zero-copy-transfer","content":"`MAPPED`"},"3797":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#segmentmode-and-zero-copy-transfer","content":"Uses memory-mapped files for segment access."},"3798":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#segmentmode-and-zero-copy-transfer","content":"`FILE_CHANNEL`"},"3799":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#segmentmode-and-zero-copy-transfer","content":"Uses standard `FileChannel` operations."},"3800":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#segmentmode-and-zero-copy-transfer","content":"For high-performance data movement, `transferTo` utilizes `FileChannel.transferTo` to move bytes directly from the file cache to a `WritableByteChannel` without copying data through the JVM heap `PartitionLog.kt:173-175`."},"3801":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#data-integrity-and-recovery-properties","content":"The log ensures consistency across restarts by scanning the partition directory and rebuilding the segment list from existing `.log` files `PartitionLog.kt:238-245`. The `LogPropertiesTest` verifies that a reopened log recovers exactly the same records and offsets as the original session `LogPropertiesTest.kt:97-103`. Additionally, the `truncateTo` operation on a `LogSegment` allows for precise data removal, ensuring that the log remains consistent by reusing the freed offset for subsequent appends `LogPropertiesTest.kt:147-151`."},"3802":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#partitionlog-boundary-and-error-invariants","content":"The implementation enforces several strict invariants to prevent corruption and resource leaks:"},"3803":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#partitionlog-boundary-and-error-invariants","content":"**Record Size Limits:** A record that is larger than an empty segment is rejected immediately to prevent the creation of \"stray\" empty files `PartitionLog.kt:64-65`."},"3804":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-25","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#partitionlog-boundary-and-error-invariants","content":"**Segment Rolling:** The log automatically rolls to a new segment when the current `activeSegment` cannot accommodate a new record `PartitionLog.kt:75`."},"3805":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-26","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#partitionlog-boundary-and-error-invariants","content":"**Boundary Integrity:** Tests confirm that records are readable even when they span across segment boundaries and that `transferTo` never attempts to cross a segment boundary in a single call `PartitionLogTest.kt:84-96`."},"3806":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-27","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"File"},"3807":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-28","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3808":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-29","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3809":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-30","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"`…/storage/PartitionLog.kt`"},"3810":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-31","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"`33-40`"},"3811":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-32","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"Primary `PartitionLog` class definition and constructor"},"3812":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-33","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"`…/storage/PartitionLog.kt`"},"3813":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-34","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"`132-138`"},"3814":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-35","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"`FetchSlice` inner class for managing segment claims"},"3815":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-36","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"`…/storage/PartitionLogTest.kt`"},"3816":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-37","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"`32-48`"},"3817":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-38","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"Tests for segment rolling and offset accuracy"},"3818":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-39","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"`…/storage/LogPropertiesTest.kt`"},"3819":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-40","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"`43-80`"},"3820":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-41","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"Randomized property-based testing for data integrity"},"3821":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-42","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"`…/benchmark/PartitionWriterBenchmark.kt`"},"3822":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-43","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"`92-102`"},"3823":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-44","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#key-files","content":"Benchmark for append performance and retention overhead"},"3824":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-45","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"`PartitionLog.append` will throw an `IllegalArgumentException` if a record is too large for a segment, rather than attempting to roll a new segment first `PartitionLog.kt:72-74`."},"3825":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-46","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"When a segment is unlinked via `retire`, a reader holding a `FetchSlice` can continue to read the data until the slice is closed, thanks to POSIX file descriptor behavior `PartitionLog.kt:28-30`."},"3826":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog-47","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/partitionlog#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"`PartitionLog.open` performs a directory scan to recover state, which can be a significant startup cost for logs with many segments `StartupProbe.kt:42-48`."},"3827":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","type":"page","content":"Recovery after a crash","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-core"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash"},"3828":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"3829":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#the-recovery-mechanism","content":"The recovery mechanism"},"3830":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#segmentmode-and-the-end-of-log-sentinel","content":"SegmentMode and the end-of-log sentinel"},"3831":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#torn-records-and-checksum-verification","content":"Torn records and checksum verification"},"3832":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#sparseoffsetindex-reconstruction","content":"SparseOffsetIndex reconstruction"},"3833":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#crashrecoverytest-invariants","content":"CrashRecoveryTest invariants"},"3834":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#recoverytest-edge-cases","content":"RecoveryTest edge cases"},"3835":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"Key files"},"3836":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"Behaviour that surprises"},"3837":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-15, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"3838":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#the-recovery-mechanism","content":"When a segment is opened, `LogSegment.open` invokes the `recover` function to reconstruct the state of the log from the raw bytes on disk (`LogSegment.kt:261-373`). This process involves walking the file by reading record headers in chunks (using a 1 MiB `RECOVERY_BUFFER` as seen in `LogSegment.kt:327`) to find valid record boundaries. As the function traverses the file, it populates the `SparseOffsetIndex` by calling `index.append` for each valid record found (`LogSegment.kt:368`)."},"3839":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#segmentmode-and-the-end-of-log-sentinel","content":"The definition of the \"end of the log\" depends on the `SegmentMode` used, which determines how the `limit` for recovery is calculated (`LogSegment.kt:285`):"},"3840":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#segmentmode-and-the-end-of-log-sentinel","content":"Mode"},"3841":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#segmentmode-and-the-end-of-log-sentinel","content":"End-of-log Sentinel"},"3842":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#segmentmode-and-the-end-of-log-sentinel","content":"`FILE_CHANNEL`"},"3843":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#segmentmode-and-the-end-of-log-sentinel","content":"The physical file length (`readChannel.size()`)"},"3844":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#segmentmode-and-the-end-of-log-sentinel","content":"`MAPPED`"},"3845":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#segmentmode-and-the-end-of-log-sentinel","content":"A zero-length prefix in a pre-sized file"},"3846":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#segmentmode-and-the-end-of-log-sentinel","content":"In `MAPPED` mode, because the file is pre-sized to its full capacity (`LogSegment.kt:288`), the recovery process must rely on finding a zero length or a checksum mismatch to stop, rather than the file size (`LogSegment.kt:349`)."},"3847":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#torn-records-and-checksum-verification","content":"To handle crashes that occur during a write, the recovery process uses CRC32C checksums stored in the `RECORD_HEADER` (`SegmentWriter.kt:85`). During recovery, the `verify` function checks the payload against the expected CRC (`LogSegment.kt:405`). If a record's body was only partially written, the checksum will fail, and recovery will treat that point as the end of the log. However, there is a known gap: if a torn write occurs *inside* a record body, it is only detectable if the checksum is verified; without it, the length prefix alone is the only evidence of integrity (`LogSegment.kt:258`)."},"3848":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#sparseoffsetindex-reconstruction","content":"The `SparseOffsetIndex` is rebuilt by scanning the log and adding entries only when the `intervalBytes` threshold is crossed (`SparseOffsetIndex.kt:73`). During recovery or manual truncation, the index is updated via `truncateTo`, which discards all entries at or above the specified offset to ensure the index does not describe data that no longer exists in the segment (`SparseOffsetIndex.kt:103`)."},"3849":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#crashrecoverytest-invariants","content":"The `CrashRecoveryTest` ensures that the system remains consistent even after a `SIGKILL`. It spawns a `CrashWriter` as a separate subprocess to simulate a hard crash (`CrashRecoveryTest.kt:56`). The core invariant verified is that after reopening the segment, the log must end on a valid record boundary, meaning every reported record is readable and matches its original checksum (`CrashRecoveryTest.kt:106`)."},"3850":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#recoverytest-edge-cases","content":"The `RecoveryTest` suite validates several critical recovery scenarios:"},"3851":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#recoverytest-edge-cases","content":"**Offset Restoration:** Ensuring that reopening a segment restores the `nextOffset` and the index correctly (`RecoveryTest.kt:38`)."},"3852":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#recoverytest-edge-cases","content":"**MAPPED Mode Orphans:** In `MAPPED` mode, if a crash leaves an \"orphaned body\" (data written but the header not yet reached), the recovery mechanism must correctly discard it by treating the missing header as the end of the log (`RecoveryTest.kt:98`)."},"3853":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-25","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"File"},"3854":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-26","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3855":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-27","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3856":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-28","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"`…/storage/LogSegment.kt`"},"3857":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-29","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"`321-373`"},"3858":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-30","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"The `recover` function implementation"},"3859":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-31","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"`…/storage/SparseOffsetIndex.kt`"},"3860":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-32","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"`71-85`"},"3861":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-33","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"Logic for appending entries to the sparse index"},"3862":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-34","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"`…/storage/SegmentWriter.kt`"},"3863":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-35","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"`85-86`"},"3864":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-36","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"Definition of the `RECORD_HEADER`"},"3865":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-37","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"`…/storage/CrashRecoveryTest.kt`"},"3866":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-38","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"`134-163`"},"3867":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-39","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"The `CrashWriter` subprocess implementation"},"3868":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-40","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"`…/storage/RecoveryTest.kt`"},"3869":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-41","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"`87-106`"},"3870":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-42","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#key-files","content":"Tests for `MAPPED` mode edge cases"},"3871":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-43","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"`LogSegment.open` in `MAPPED` mode may pre-size the file to its full capacity, meaning the file size on disk does not represent the amount of data actually written (`LogSegment.kt:282`)."},"3872":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-44","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"The `SparseOffsetIndex` is not dense; it only stores an entry every `intervalBytes`, requiring a forward scan to find exact positions (`SparseOffsetIndex.kt:18`)."},"3873":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash-45","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core/recovery-after-crash#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"`SegmentWriter.append` is not thread-safe by design; it assumes a single-threaded ownership by a single coroutine (`SegmentWriter.kt:15`)."},"3874":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","type":"page","content":"Command-line verbs","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-conformance"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs"},"3875":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"3876":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-capabilities-verb","content":"The `capabilities` verb"},"3877":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-metadata-verb","content":"The `metadata` verb"},"3878":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-produce-verb-and-ackpolicy","content":"The `produce` verb and `AckPolicy`"},"3879":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-produce-keyed-verb-and-partitionerfnv1a","content":"The `produce-keyed` verb and `Partitioner.Fnv1a`"},"3880":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-fetch-verb-and-maxbytes-truncation","content":"The `fetch` verb and `maxBytes` truncation"},"3881":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#exit-codes-and-errorcode-reporting","content":"Exit codes and `ErrorCode` reporting"},"3882":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#key-files","content":"Key files"},"3883":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"Behaviour that surprise"},"3884":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `ef58254ca7be`, 2026-08-16, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"3885":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-capabilities-verb","content":"The handshake mechanism where the client declares its roles (producer, consumer) and name. The client must respond with `roles=` and `name=` to allow the harness to determine which checks to run `Main.kt:43-46`."},"3886":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-metadata-verb","content":"Retrieving topic information, including partition IDs, log start offsets, and high watermarks. The client iterates through the topics and partitions returned by the broker to print `partition=<id> <start_offset> <high_watermark>` `Main.kt:98-104`."},"3887":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-produce-verb-and-ackpolicy","content":"Mechanics of sending records and the behavior of `AckPolicy.NONE` (silent requests) versus `WRITTEN` and `FORCED`. The `ack` argument is mapped to an `AckPolicy` as follows:"},"3888":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-produce-verb-and-ackpolicy","content":"Argument"},"3889":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-produce-verb-and-ackpolicy","content":"`AckPolicy`"},"3890":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-produce-verb-and-ackpolicy","content":"Behavior"},"3891":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-produce-verb-and-ackpolicy","content":"`none`"},"3892":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-produce-verb-and-ackpolicy","content":"`AckPolicy.NONE`"},"3893":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-produce-verb-and-ackpolicy","content":"No response is expected; the client returns immediately `Main.kt:117`"},"3894":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-produce-verb-and-ackpolicy","content":"`written`"},"3895":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-produce-verb-and-ackpolicy","content":"`AckPolicy.WRITTEN`"},"3896":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-produce-verb-and-ackpolicy","content":"Client waits for a response `Main.kt:118`"},"3897":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-produce-verb-and-ackpolicy","content":"`forced`"},"3898":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-produce-verb-and-ackpolicy","content":"`AckPolicy.FORCED`"},"3899":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-produce-verb-and-ackpolicy","content":"Client waits for a response `Main.kt:119`"},"3900":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-25","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-produce-keyed-verb-and-partitionerfnv1a","content":"How the client-side partitioner selects a partition based on a key before the broker sees the data. The client first fetches metadata to find available partitions and then uses `Partitioner.Fnv1a.partitionFor` to select the target partition `Main.kt:158`."},"3901":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-26","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#the-fetch-verb-and-maxbytes-truncation","content":"Retrieving records, handling the high watermark, and the edge case where a record exceeds `maxBytes` resulting in a truncated tail. If a response contains no complete records but the `truncated` flag is set, the client reports the `truncatedRecordBytes` `Main.kt:182-184`."},"3902":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-27","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#exit-codes-and-errorcode-reporting","content":"Distinguishing between client-side failures (non-zero exit) and broker-side refusals (exit zero with `error=CODE`). A broker refusal is considered a valid result and is reported via `error=CODE` on stdout `Main.kt:84-85`, whereas a client-side exception results in a non-zero exit code `Main.kt:86`."},"3903":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-28","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#key-files","content":"File"},"3904":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-29","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3905":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-30","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3906":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs-31","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-conformance/command-line-verbs","t