otocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#errorcode-and-request-failure-modes","content":"Unknown `apiKey` or `apiVersion`"},"4426":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-60","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#errorcode-and-request-failure-modes","content":"Echoed if header is parsed"},"4427":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-61","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#errorcode-and-request-failure-modes","content":"`CORRUPT_REQUEST`"},"4428":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-62","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#errorcode-and-request-failure-modes","content":"5"},"4429":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-63","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#errorcode-and-request-failure-modes","content":"Frame is malformed or unsatisfiable"},"4430":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-64","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#errorcode-and-request-failure-modes","content":"Echoed if header is parsed; otherwise 0"},"4431":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-65","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#requestdecoder-and-frame-validation","content":"The `RequestDecoder` is responsible for transforming raw bytes into structured `Request` objects. It performs rigorous bounds-checking to ensure that a remote party cannot cause memory issues, as seen in `Requests.kt:79-132`. Key validation mechanics include:"},"4432":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-66","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#requestdecoder-and-frame-validation","content":"**Header Integrity**: The `correlationId` is read first so it can be echoed even if the body is corrupt (`Requests.kt:93-96`)."},"4433":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-67","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#requestdecoder-and-frame-validation","content":"**Unsatisfiable Constraints**: In `decodeFetch`, if `minBytes > maxBytes`, a `CorruptRequestException` is thrown because the request can never be satisfied (`Requests.kt:209-210`)."},"4434":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-68","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#requestdecoder-and-frame-validation","content":"**Positive Counts**: `recordCount` in `PRODUCE` and `topicCount` in `METADATA` must be non-negative and must not exceed the remaining bytes in the buffer (`Requests.kt:149`, `Requests.kt:176`)."},"4435":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-69","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#partial-frame-assembly-and-socket-resilience","content":"The protocol is designed to handle fragmented network delivery. `PartialFrameTest.kt:29-40` demonstrates that a frame split across multiple packets (e.g., sending the length prefix, waiting, then sending the tail) is correctly assembled by the session. Furthermore, the protocol ensures connection resilience: if a frame is well-formed but contains an invalid `ApiKey` or `apiVersion`, the broker responds with an error but keeps the connection open (`ErrorCodeTest.kt:32-41`)."},"4436":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-70","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#frame-length-limits-and-resource-protection","content":"To prevent Denial of Service (DoS) attacks where an attacker sends a massive `int32` length prefix to force large memory allocations, the broker enforces a strict limit. As tested in `PartialFrameTest.kt:112-129`, if a frame length exceeds the allowed bounds, the broker drops the connection immediately rather than attempting to allocate the requested memory."},"4437":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-71","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#key-files","content":"File"},"4438":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-72","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#key-files","content":"Lines"},"4439":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-73","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#key-files","content":"What is there"},"4440":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-74","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#key-files","content":"`…/wire/Protocol.kt`"},"4441":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-75","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#key-files","content":"`15-58`"},"4442":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-76","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#key-files","content":"Protocol constants, `ApiKey` enum, and `ErrorCode` enum."},"4443":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-77","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#key-files","content":"`…/net/PartialFrameTest.kt`"},"4444":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-78","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#key-files","content":"`40-62`"},"4445":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-79","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#key-files","content":"Tests for split packets and frame assembly."},"4446":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-80","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#key-files","content":"`…/net/ErrorCodeTest.kt`"},"4447":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-81","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#key-files","content":"`32-51`"},"4448":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-82","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#key-files","content":"Tests for error code responses and correlationId echoing."},"4449":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-83","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#key-files","content":"`…/wire/Requests.kt`"},"4450":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-84","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#key-files","content":"`79-132`"},"4451":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-85","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#key-files","content":"The `RequestDecoder` implementation and validation logic."},"4452":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-86","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**CorrelationId Zeroing**: If a frame is so short that the `correlationId` cannot be parsed, the broker returns `0` as the ID in the error response (`ErrorCodeTest.kt:78-81`)."},"4453":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-87","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**Zero-Copy and CRC**: The broker does not calculate the CRC for `FETCH` responses because it uses `transferTo` to move data directly from the disk to the socket, bypassing the heap (`protocol-wire.md:154-156`)."},"4454":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and-88","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-protocol/protocol-constants-and#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**Unsatisfiable Fetch**: A `FETCH` request where `minBytes` is greater than `maxBytes` is rejected during decoding as a `CORRUPT_REQUEST` because it is logically impossible to satisfy (`Requests.kt:209-210`)."},"4455":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","type":"page","content":"BooblikServer","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-net"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver"},"4456":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"What this module is responsible for"},"4457":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"4458":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#transport-modes-selector-vs-virtual_threads","content":"Transport Modes: SELECTOR vs VIRTUAL_THREADS"},"4459":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#fetchmode-zero_copy-and-the-filechannel-path","content":"FetchMode: ZERO_COPY and the FileChannel Path"},"4460":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#the-acceptor-loop-and-connection-lifecycle","content":"The Acceptor Loop and Connection Lifecycle"},"4461":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#session-failure-domains-and-supervisorjob","content":"Session Failure Domains and SupervisorJob"},"4462":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#the-m-64-bind-address-fix","content":"The M-64 Bind Address Fix"},"4463":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#server-configuration-and-tcp-options","content":"Server Configuration and TCP Options"},"4464":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"Key files"},"4465":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"Behaviour that surprises"},"4466":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-15, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"4467":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"The `BooblikServer` acts as the network front end of the broker, managing the lifecycle of connections and dispatching requests to the appropriate partitions. It provides two distinct transport mechanisms and supports zero-copy data transfer for high-performance fetching."},"4468":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#transport-modes-selector-vs-virtual_threads","content":"The server supports two different execution models for handling connections, which can be configured via `ServerConfig` (`BooblikServer.kt:59`):"},"4469":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#transport-modes-selector-vs-virtual_threads","content":"Mode"},"4470":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#transport-modes-selector-vs-virtual_threads","content":"Mechanism"},"4471":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#transport-modes-selector-vs-virtual_threads","content":"Implementation Detail"},"4472":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#transport-modes-selector-vs-virtual_threads","content":"`SELECTOR`"},"4473":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#transport-modes-selector-vs-virtual_threads","content":"NIO-based selector loop"},"4474":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#transport-modes-selector-vs-virtual_threads","content":"Uses `SelectorLoop` to manage readiness and one coroutine per connection (`BooblikServer.kt:150-188`)"},"4475":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#transport-modes-selector-vs-virtual_threads","content":"`VIRTUAL_THREADS`"},"4476":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#transport-modes-selector-vs-virtual_threads","content":"Thread-per-connection"},"4477":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#transport-modes-selector-vs-virtual_threads","content":"Uses a `VirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor` where `runBlocking` turns suspension points into thread parks (`BooblikServer.kt:200-218`)"},"4478":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#fetchmode-zero_copy-and-the-filechannel-path","content":"To achieve high performance, the server provides two ways to deliver data to the client (`BooblikServer.kt:37-43`):"},"4479":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#fetchmode-zero_copy-and-the-filechannel-path","content":"Mode"},"4480":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#fetchmode-zero_copy-and-the-filechannel-path","content":"Mechanism"},"4481":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-25","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#fetchmode-zero_copy-and-the-filechannel-path","content":"Description"},"4482":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-26","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#fetchmode-zero_copy-and-the-filechannel-path","content":"`ZERO_COPY`"},"4483":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-27","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#fetchmode-zero_copy-and-the-filechannel-path","content":"`sendfile`"},"4484":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-28","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#fetchmode-zero_copy-and-the-filechannel-path","content":"Uses `FileChannel.transferTo` to move data from the page cache directly to the socket buffer, bypassing the JVM heap (`BooblikServer.kt:113-115`)"},"4485":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-29","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#fetchmode-zero_copy-and-the-filechannel-path","content":"`HEAP`"},"4486":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-30","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#fetchmode-zero_copy-and-the-filechannel-path","content":"Heap Buffer"},"4487":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-31","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#fetchmode-zero_copy-and-the-filechannel-path","content":"Reads data into a heap buffer and then writes it, serving as the control group for experiments (`BooblikServer.kt:41-42`)"},"4488":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-32","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#the-acceptor-loop-and-connection-lifecycle","content":"The server maintains an acceptor loop that is responsible for accepting new `SocketChannel` instances. In `SELECTOR` mode, this loop is a coroutine running within a `SupervisorJob` (`BooblikServer.kt:154-159`). The loop is designed to be resilient: if an exception occurs during `serverChannel.accept()`, it is treated as transient, the error is recorded in `metrics`, and the loop continues to prevent the broker from hanging silently (`BooblikServer.kt:169-175`)."},"4489":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-33","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#session-failure-domains-and-supervisorjob","content":"To ensure high availability, each client connection is isolated within its own coroutine scope. By using a `SupervisorJob` (`BooblikServer.kt:123-124`), the server ensures that a failure in a single `Session` (such as a malformed request or a sudden connection drop) only terminates that specific session and does not propagate upwards to crash the entire `BooblikServer` (`BooblikServer.kt:185-187`)."},"4490":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-34","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#the-m-64-bind-address-fix","content":"A critical correctness feature is the ability to bind to a specific `bindAddress` rather than a wildcard address (`BooblikServer.kt:58`). As documented in `ServerFixture.kt:40-46`, binding to a specific address like `127.0.0.1` prevents \"silent connection theft\" on BSD-derived systems where `SO_REUSEADDR` might allow another process to intercept connections intended for the broker if a wildcard bind is used."},"4491":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-35","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#server-configuration-and-tcp-options","content":"The server applies specific socket options to optimize the transport layer (`BooblikServer.kt:227-233`):"},"4492":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-36","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#server-configuration-and-tcp-options","content":"Option"},"4493":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-37","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#server-configuration-and-tcp-options","content":"Purpose"},"4494":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-38","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#server-configuration-and-tcp-options","content":"`TCP_NODELAY`"},"4495":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-39","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#server-configuration-and-tcp-options","content":"Disables Nagle's algorithm to reduce latency for small batches (`BooblikServer.kt:228`)"},"4496":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-40","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#server-configuration-and-tcp-options","content":"`SO_KEEPALIVE`"},"4497":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-41","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#server-configuration-and-tcp-options","content":"Enabled to ensure that connections held open for long periods (e.g., during a `FETCH`) are detected as failed by the OS rather than remaining silent (`BooblikServer.kt:232`)"},"4498":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-42","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"File"},"4499":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-43","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"Lines"},"4500":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-44","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"What is there"},"4501":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-45","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"`…/net/BooblikServer.kt`"},"4502":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-46","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"`25-64`"},"4503":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-47","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"`ServerConfig` and `Transport`/`FetchMode` enums"},"4504":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-48","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"`…/net/BooblikServer.kt`"},"4505":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-49","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"`117-147`"},"4506":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-50","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"`BooblikServer` class and `start()` method"},"4507":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-51","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"`…/net/BooblikServer.kt`"},"4508":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-52","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"`149-197`"},"4509":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-53","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"`startSelector` implementation and acceptor loop"},"4510":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-54","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"`…/net/BooblikServer.kt`"},"4511":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-55","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"`199-225`"},"4512":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-56","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"`startVirtualThreads` implementation"},"4513":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-57","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"`…/net/BooblikServer.kt`"},"4514":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-58","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"`235-251`"},"4515":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-59","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#key-files","content":"`serve` method and session lifecycle"},"4516":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-60","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"The `startSelector` loop is designed to catch `Exception` and continue (`BooblikServer.kt:169`) to avoid a \"silent hang\" where the process is alive but the port is unresponsive."},"4517":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-61","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"In `startVirtualThreads`, the code uses `runBlocking` inside a virtual thread (`BooblikServer.kt:218`) specifically to allow the same `serve` logic to be used for both `SELECTOR` and `VIRTUAL_THREADS` transports."},"4518":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver-62","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/booblikserver#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"The `close` method performs a coordinated shutdown of the `serverChannel`, `acceptorThread`, `virtualThreads`, and the `scope` (`BooblikServer.kt:253-260`)."},"4519":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","type":"page","content":"FetchMode","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-net"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode"},"4520":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"What this module is responsible for"},"4521":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"4522":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetchmode","content":"FetchMode"},"4523":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#zero_copy-mechanics","content":"ZERO_COPY mechanics"},"4524":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#heap-staging-and-buffer-reuse","content":"HEAP staging and buffer reuse"},"4525":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetch-slice-lifecycle-and-retention","content":"Fetch slice lifecycle and retention"},"4526":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetch-response-integrity-and-truncation","content":"Fetch response integrity and truncation"},"4527":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#key-files","content":"Key files"},"4528":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"Behaviour that surprises"},"4529":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-15, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"4530":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"The `FetchMode` determines the data transfer strategy used by the broker to move log data from the storage layer to the network socket during a `FetchRequest`. It is a critical performance knob that dictates whether data passes through the JVM heap or stays within the OS page cache."},"4531":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetchmode","content":"The available strategies are defined in `BooblikServer.kt:37-43`:"},"4532":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetchmode","content":"Mode"},"4533":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetchmode","content":"Description"},"4534":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetchmode","content":"`ZERO_COPY`"},"4535":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetchmode","content":"Uses `FileChannel.transferTo` to move data from the page cache directly to the socket buffer, bypassing the JVM heap."},"4536":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetchmode","content":"`HEAP`"},"4537":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetchmode","content":"Reads data into a heap-allocated staging buffer before writing it to the connection."},"4538":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#zero_copy-mechanics","content":"When `FetchMode.ZERO_COPY` is selected, the `Session` utilizes the `Connection.transferFrom` method to perform a zero-copy transfer `Session.kt:221-223`. This approach leverages the operating system's ability to move data from the file system cache directly to the network stack, avoiding the overhead of copying bytes into the application's memory space."},"4539":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#heap-staging-and-buffer-reuse","content":"In `HEAP` mode, the `Session` manages a reusable staging buffer to minimize allocation pressure `Session.kt:289-294`. The lifecycle of this buffer is as follows:"},"4540":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#heap-staging-and-buffer-reuse","content":"**Allocation**: A buffer is allocated with an initial size of 64 KiB `Session.kt:297`."},"4541":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#heap-staging-and-buffer-reuse","content":"**Growth**: If a request requires more space, the `staging` function allocates a new `ByteBuffer` of the required size `Session.kt:290`."},"4542":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#heap-staging-and-buffer-reuse","content":"**Reuse**: The same buffer is cleared and reused for subsequent requests to avoid frequent GC cycles."},"4543":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetch-slice-lifecycle-and-retention","content":"To prevent a long-running `FetchRequest` from blocking log retention, the `Session` manages data access through a \"slice\" mechanism `Session.kt:206`."},"4544":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetch-slice-lifecycle-and-retention","content":"**Opening**: A slice is opened only after the `maxWaitMillis` period has passed and the `highWatermark` is checked `Session.kt:188`."},"4545":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-25","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetch-slice-lifecycle-and-retention","content":"**Retention**: The slice is held open only during the actual I/O operation (the header and the body) `Session.kt:212`."},"4546":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-26","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetch-slice-lifecycle-and-retention","content":"**Closing**: The slice is automatically closed via a `use` block, ensuring that the log segment is not held open longer than necessary, which would otherwise prevent the retention policy from deleting old segments `Session.kt:212`."},"4547":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-27","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetch-response-integrity-and-truncation","content":"The server ensures that responses respect the `maxBytes` constraint and segment boundaries:"},"4548":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-28","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetch-response-integrity-and-truncation","content":"**Truncation**: If a record is cut off by the `maxBytes` limit, the `Session` marks the response as truncated `ServerTest.kt:117`."},"4549":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-29","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetch-response-integrity-and-truncation","content":"**Segment Boundaries**: A fetch operation will stop at a segment boundary; if a request spans multiple segments, the client must perform subsequent fetches to retrieve data from the next segment `ServerTest.kt:137`."},"4550":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-30","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#fetch-response-integrity-and-truncation","content":"**Integrity**: The `maxBytes` constraint is applied to the total bytes returned, and the `truncated` flag is used to signal to the client that the full record was not sent `ServerTest.kt:117`."},"4551":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-31","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#key-files","content":"File"},"4552":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-32","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#key-files","content":"Lines"},"4553":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-33","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#key-files","content":"What is there"},"4554":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-34","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#key-files","content":"`…/net/BooblikServer.kt`"},"4555":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-35","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#key-files","content":"`37-43`"},"4556":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-36","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#key-files","content":"The `FetchMode` enum defining `ZERO_COPY` and `HEAP`."},"4557":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-37","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#key-files","content":"`…/net/Session.kt`"},"4558":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-38","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#key-files","content":"`219-231`"},"4559":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-39","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#key-files","content":"The implementation of the `fetch` logic for both `ZERO_COPY` and `HEAP` modes."},"4560":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-40","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#key-files","content":"`…/net/ServerTest.kt`"},"4561":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-41","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode#key-files","content":"`105-122`"},"4562":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-net/fetchmode-42