d":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance-14","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance#produce-operations","content":"Ack Policy"},"4955":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance-15","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance#produce-operations","content":"Mapping"},"4956":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance-16","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance#produce-operations","content":"`none`"},"4957":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance-17","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance#produce-operations","content":"`AckPolicy.None`"},"4958":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance-18","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance#produce-operations","content":"`written`"},"4959":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance-19","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance#produce-operations","content":"`AckPolicy.Written`"},"4960":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance-20","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance#produce-operations","content":"`forced`"},"4961":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance-21","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance#produce-operations","content":"`AckPolicy.Forced`"},"4962":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance-22","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance#produce-operations","content":"The `Produce` function handles hex-encoded payloads and different acknowledgment requirements `Program.cs:111-139`. Additionally, `ProduceKeyed` exercises the partitioner by using `topic.PartitionFor(key)` to determine the destination partition before sending the record `Program.cs:143-158`."},"4963":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance-23","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance#fetch-operations","content":"Retrieving records and handling edge cases like truncated tails and `maxBytes` limits. The `Fetch` function retrieves records via `connection.FetchAsync` and reports the `HighWatermark` `Program.cs:72-81`. It specifically handles cases where a response is truncated because a record exceeds the `maxBytes` limit, reporting `recordExceedsMaxBytes` `Program.cs:85-89`."},"4964":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance-24","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance#broker-refusal-handling","content":"How the client reports `BrokerException` results via stdout without exiting with error. When a `BrokerException` is caught, the program prints `error={refusal.Code.WireName()}` to `stdout` and exits with code 0, as a refusal is considered a valid result rather than a program failure `Program.cs:61-65`."},"4965":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance-25","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance#key-files","content":"File"},"4966":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance-26","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance#key-files","content":"Lines"},"4967":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance-27","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik.Conformance","tags":[],"type"