mer-32","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#the-fetched-record-structure","content":"`Records`"},"5394":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-33","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#the-fetched-record-structure","content":"The list of successfully decoded records"},"5395":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-34","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#the-fetched-record-structure","content":"`Truncated`"},"5396":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-35","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#the-fetched-record-structure","content":"Indicates if the response ended inside a record due to `maxBytes` limits `Consumer.cs:19`"},"5397":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-36","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#the-fetched-record-structure","content":"`TruncatedRecordBytes`"},"5398":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-37","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#the-fetched-record-structure","content":"The size of the dropped record if `Truncated` is true `Consumer.cs:20`"},"5399":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-38","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#the-fetched-record-structure","content":"The response frame contains a \"promised\" payload length which is checked against the actual received bytes to detect if the response was cut short by a broker restart `Consumer.cs:176-180`."},"5400":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-39","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#consumer-position-and-lag","content":"The `Consumer` manages the local read position, which is the offset of the next record to be read `Consumer.cs:55`."},"5401":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-40","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#consumer-position-and-lag","content":"**Position**: The offset the consumer is currently at. It is advanced only after a successful poll `Consumer.cs:106`."},"5402":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-41","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#consumer-position-and-lag","content":"**HighWatermark**: A snapshot of the log end at the last poll `Consumer.cs:60`."},"5403":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-42","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#consumer-position-and-lag","content":"**Lag**: Calculated as the difference between the `HighWatermark` and the `Position`, ensuring it never returns a negative value `Consumer.cs:64`."},"5404":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-43","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#pollasync-and-recordsasync","content":"The consumer provides two ways to consume data:"},"5405":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-44","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#pollasync-and-recordsasync","content":"**`PollAsync`**: A discrete method that fetches a batch of records and advances the `Position` `Consumer.cs:94`."},"5406":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-45","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#pollasync-and-recordsasync","content":"**`RecordsAsync`**: An `IAsyncEnumerable` stream that yields records one at a time `Consumer.cs:139`. This interface applies back-pressure because the next fetch does not occur until the loop body is finished `Consumer.cs:131`."},"5407":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-46","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#pollasync-and-recordsasync","content":"An empty list returned by a poll is not an end-of-log signal, but a steady state for a caught-up consumer `Consumer.cs:78`."},"5408":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-47","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#record-checksum-verification","content":"The decoding process involves unframing the `FETCH` response and verifying the integrity of every record `Consumer.cs:155`."},"5409":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-48","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#record-checksum-verification","content":"**CRC32C Validation**: Every record is checked using `Crc32C.Compute(record)` against the stored checksum `Consumer.cs:214-217`."},"5410":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-49","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#record-checksum-verification","content":"**`CorruptRecordException`**: Thrown when the computed checksum does not match the stored one `Consumer.cs:217`."},"5411":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-50","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#record-checksum-verification","content":"**`RecordExceedsMaxBytesException`**: Thrown when a response is truncated and the next record's size exceeds the consumer's `MaxBytes` limit, causing a potential stall `Consumer.cs:102`."},"5412":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-51","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#subscription-cost-and-long-fetch","content":"The performance of a consumer depends on its polling strategy, which is measured by the ratio of request frequency to broker load `SubscriptionProbe.kt:37-41`."},"5413":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-52","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#subscription-cost-and-long-fetch","content":"Strategy"},"5414":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-53","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#subscription-cost-and-long-fetch","content":"Mechanism"},"5415":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-54","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tag