 `Main.kt:79-83`."},"5444":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-83","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"`Consumer.RecordsAsync` is an `IAsyncEnumerable` that applies back-pressure by construction; the next fetch does not happen until the consumer's loop body is complete `Consumer.cs:131`."},"5445":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer-84","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/fetchasync-and-consumer#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"A response that is truncated because it hits the `maxBytes` limit is not considered a corruption, but a routine event `Consumer.cs:212`."},"5446":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","type":"page","content":"clients/dotnet/Booblik","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","clients/dotnet/Booblik"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik"},"5447":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-0","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"5448":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-1","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#connection","content":"Connection"},"5449":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-2","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#metadata-and-topic-discovery","content":"Metadata and Topic Discovery"},"5450":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-3","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#produceasync-and-ackpolicy","content":"ProduceAsync and AckPolicy"},"5451":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-4","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","type":"h