:{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-12","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#connection","content":"More: Connection"},"5460":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-13","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#metadata-and-topic-discovery","content":"Retrieving partition information and topic existence from the broker. The `MetadataAsync` method sends a request containing a list of topic names and decodes the response into a dictionary of partition information `Connection.cs:145`. Users can also use `TopicAsync` to get a `Topic` object which encapsulates the partitions available for a specific name `Connection.cs:292`."},"5461":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-14","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#produceasync-and-ackpolicy","content":"Appending records to a partition and managing durability guarantees via `AckPolicy`. The `ProduceAsync` method allows sending a list of records to a specific partition `Connection.cs:183`. The durability of the write is determined by the following table:"},"5462":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-15","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#produceasync-and-ackpolicy","content":"AckPolicy"},"5463":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-16","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#produceasync-and-ackpolicy","content":"Value"},"5464":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-17","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#produceasync-and-ackpolicy","content":"Description"},"5465":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-18","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#produceasync-and-ackpolicy","content":"`None`"},"5466":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-19","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#produceasync-and-ackpolicy","content":"0"},"5467":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-20","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#produceasync-and-ackpolicy","content":"Answers nothing; the broker may lose the record without the client knowing `Connection.cs:15`"},"5468":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-21","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#produceasync-and-ackpolicy","content":"`Written`"},"5469":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-22","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#produceasync-and-ackpolicy","content":"1"},"5470":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-23","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#produceasync-and-ackpolicy","content":"Answers once the record is in the log, before any durability barrier `Connection.cs:18`"},"5471":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-24","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#produceasync-and-ackpolicy","content":"`Forced`"},"5472":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-25","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#produceasync-and-ackpolicy","content":"2"},"5473":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-26","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#produceasync-and-ackpolicy","content":"Answers after the broker's `force()` operation `Connection.cs:21`"},"5474":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-27","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#produceasync-and-ackpolicy","content":"More: ProduceAsync and AckPolicy"},"5475":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-28","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#fetchasync-and-consumer","content":"Reading records from a partition, handling truncation, and managing the consumer position. The `Consumer` class maintains a `Position` which is the offset of the next record to be read `Consumer.cs:55`. The `PollAsync` method fetches records and advances the position, but it can throw a `RecordExceedsMaxBytesException` if a record is too large to fit within the `MaxBytes` limit `Consumer.cs:94`."},"5476":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-29","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#fetchasync-and-consumer","content":"More: FetchAsync and Consumer"},"5477":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-30","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#topic-partitioning","content":"Using FNV-1a hashing to map keys to specific partitions. The `Partitioner` class provides the `Fnv1a32` hash function which uses an `unchecked` context to allow arithmetic wrapping `Partitioner.cs:33`. The `PartitionFor` method then folds this hash into the range of available partitions using the modulo operator `Partitioner.cs:54`."},"5478":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-31","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#crc32c-verification","content":"Checksum validation for record integrity using the Castagnoli polynomial. The `Crc32C` class implements the CRC-32C algorithm using a pre-computed table for efficiency `Crc32C.cs:34`. This is used during the `Decode` process in a `Consumer` to ensure that the bytes received match the checksum stored with the record `Consumer.cs:214`."},"5479":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-32","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#error-handling-and-protocol-exceptions","content":"Distinguishing between broker refusals, protocol violations, and data corruption. The client distinguishes between different failure modes:"},"5480":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-33","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#error-handling-and-protocol-exceptions","content":"Exception"},"5481":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-34","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#error-handling-and-protocol-exceptions","content":"Type"},"5482":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-35","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#error-handling-and-protocol-exceptions","content":"Cause"},"5483":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-36","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#error-handling-and-protocol-exceptions","content":"`BrokerException`"},"5484":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-37","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#error-handling-and-protocol-exceptions","content":"Refusal"},"5485":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-38","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#error-handling-and-protocol-exceptions","content":"The broker understood the request but declined it (e.g., `UnknownTopicOrPartition`) `Errors.cs:35`"},"5486":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-39","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#error-handling-and-protocol-exceptions","content":"`ProtocolException`"},"5487":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-40","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik#error-handling-and-protocol-exceptions","content":"Violation"},"5488":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik-41",