d-ackpolicy#ackpolicy","content":"Mode"},"5529":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-12","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#ackpolicy","content":"Value"},"5530":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-13","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#ackpolicy","content":"Description"},"5531":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-14","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#ackpolicy","content":"`None`"},"5532":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-15","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#ackpolicy","content":"0"},"5533":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-16","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#ackpolicy","content":"The broker answers nothing; the client receives no response and no offset."},"5534":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-17","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#ackpolicy","content":"`Written`"},"5535":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-18","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#ackpolicy","content":"1"},"5536":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-19","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#ackpolicy","content":"The broker answers once the record is in the log, before any durability barrier."},"5537":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-20","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#ackpolicy","content":"`Forced`"},"5538":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-21","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#ackpolicy","content":"2"},"5539":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-22","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#ackpolicy","content":"The broker answers after a `force()` operation (grouping all queued requests)."},"5540":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-23","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#ackpolicy","content":"`Connection.cs:8-22`"},"5541":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-24","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#produceasync-mechanics","content":"The `ProduceAsync` method constructs a binary payload containing the topic name, partition ID, the chosen `AckPolicy`, and the list of records. The records are written to the partition such that they land contiguously, meaning one request results in a sequence of offsets from `BaseOffset` to `LogEndOffset` with no interleaving from other requests `Connection.cs:183-213`."},"5542":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-25","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#the-write-actor-and-batching","content":"Performance is heavily dependent on how records are grouped. While `Topic.SendAsync` allows sending a single record, doing so one at a time is inefficient compared to using `Connection.ProduceAsync` with a list of records `Connection.cs:382-387`. In the Kotlin implementation, the `batch` function provides a way to collect records into a `BatchScope` to ensure they are sent as a single request, bypassing the standard accumulator to maintain the guarantee that records land contiguously `Publishing.kt:85-99`."},"5543":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-26","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#failure-modes-and-brokerexception","content":"The client handles various broker responses. If a batch is empty or contains empty records, the broker may return a `CORRUPT_REQUEST` `Connection.cs:178-180`. If the broker refuses a request (e.g., `UNKNOWN_TOPIC_OR_PARTITION`), a `BrokerException` is thrown to the caller `Connection.cs:131`. Under `AckPolicy.None`, `ProduceAsync` returns `null` because no response is expected from the broker `Connection.cs:214-216`."},"5544":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-27","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#recovery-after-a-crash","content":"Writes are not atomic. If a crash occurs mid-write, the system is designed so that recovery keeps the prefix of the batch that passed its checksums, meaning a partial batch can survive on its own `Publishing.kt:76-79`."},"5545":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-28","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#connection-integrity-tests","content":"The test suite ensures high reliability through several checks:"},"5546":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-29","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#connection-integrity-tests","content":"**Byte-for-byte delivery**: Verifying that records arrive exactly as sent `ConnectionTests.cs:24-30`."},"5547":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-30","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#connection-integrity-tests","content":"**Error propagation**: Ensuring that a broker refusal is treated as a `BrokerException` but does not close the connection, allowing for reuse `ConnectionTests.cs:56-64`."},"5548":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-31","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#connection-integrity-tests","content":"**Protocol integrity**: Confirming that a truncated response (e.g., due to a broker restart) results in a `ProtocolException` `ConnectionTests.cs:100-103`."},"5549":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-32","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#key-files","content":"File"},"5550":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-33","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/c