t-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-55","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#key-files","content":"Benchmark for append performance and retention"},"5573":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-56","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#key-files","content":"`…/Booblik.Conformance/Program.cs`"},"5574":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-57","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#key-files","content":"`127-138`"},"5575":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-58","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#key-files","content":"Conformance testing for `Produce` verb and `AckPolicy.None`"},"5576":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-59","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#behaviour-that-not-obvious","content":"`Connection.ProduceAsync` returns `null` when `AckPolicy.None` is used, which can be interpreted as \"no answer is coming\" `Connection.cs:214-216`."},"5577":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-60","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#behaviour-that-not-obvious","content":"A `BrokerException` does not necessarily close the `Connection`; if the framing remains intact, the connection remains usable for subsequent requests `ConnectionTests.cs:60-64`."},"5578":{"id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy-61","page_id":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-dotnet-Booblik/produceasync-and-ackpolicy#behaviour-that-not-obvious","content":"`Topic.SendAsync` is a convenience method that wraps a single record into a list, which is significantly slower than batching multiple records in one `ProduceAsync` call `Connection.cs:382-387`."},"5579":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","type":"page","content":"CRC-32C Checksum Implementation","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","clients"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation"},"5580":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-0","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"5581":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-1","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#the-crc-32c-polynomial-and-reflected-tables","content":"The CRC-32C Polynomial and Reflected Tables"},"5582":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-2","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#the-zero-copy-read-path-and-client-side-verification","content":"The Zero-Copy Read Path and Client-Side Verification"},"5583":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-3","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#the-recovery-process-and-torn-records","content":"The Recovery Process and Torn Records"},"5584":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-4","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#language-specific-arithmetic-traps","content":"Language-Specific Arithmetic Traps"},"5585":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-5","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#conformance-and-golden-vectors","content":"Conformance and Golden Vectors"},"5586":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-6","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#key-files","content":"Key files"},"5587":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-7","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"Behaviour that surprises"},"5588":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-8","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `ef58254ca7be`, 2026-08-16, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"5589":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-9","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#the-crc-32c-polynomial-and-reflected-tables","content":"The implementation uses the Castagnoli polynomial `0x1EDC6F41`. Because many implementations, such as the one in `crc32c.js:32`, utilize right-shifting, the table must be built using the reflected form of the polynomial, which is `0x82F63B78` (`crc32c.js:25`). Using the standard polynomial with a right-shift results in a \"stable, plausible, everywhere-wrong sum\" (`crc32c.js:16`)."},"5590":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-10","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#the-zero-copy-read-path-and-client-side-verification","content":"A critical design decision in the booblik protocol is that the broker does not touch the payload bytes on the read path to enable zero-copy performance; consequently, the responsibility for verifying the checksum shifts entirely to the client (`SegmentWriter.kt:78-80`). While the broker computes the checksum on write, the client is the only party on the read path capable of performing the verification (`SegmentWriter.kt:79`)."},"5591":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-11","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#the-recovery-process-and-torn-records","content":"The checksum serves as a vital sentinel during the broker's startup recovery process. Because a length prefix alone cannot distinguish between a valid record and a partially written (torn) record after a crash, the checksum allows recovery to stop at the first record whose bytes do not match their own header (`SegmentWriter.kt:73-74`)."},"5592":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-12","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#language-specific-arithmetic-traps","content":"Different programming languages require specific handling to manage 32-bit integer arithmetic and sign bits:"},"5593":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-13","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#language-specific-arithmetic-traps","content":"**JavaScript**: Requires the `>>> 0` operator to ensure bitwise operations produce unsigned 32-bit results rather than signed ones (`crc32c.js:57`)."},"5594":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-14","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#language-specific-arithmetic-traps","content":"**Java**: Requires a cast from the `long` returned by `CRC32C.getValue()` to an `int` (`README.md:52`)."},"5595":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-15","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#language-specific-arithmetic-traps","content":"**Python**: Must handle the fact that its integers never overflow, requiring specific logic to match the expected signed/unsigned behavior (`README.md:38`)."},"5596":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-16","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#language-specific-arithmetic-traps","content":"**C#**: Does not require special handling because a cast between `int` and `uint` preserves the bits (`README.md:55`)."},"5597":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-17","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#conformance-and-golden-vectors","content":"To ensure correctness across all implementations, the module is validated against \"golden vectors\" (`README.md:37`). These vectors, stored in `conformance/vectors/crc32c.tsv`, are used to catch errors where an implementation might be self-consistent but mathematically incorrect, such as using a mis-derived reflected polynomial (`README.md:83-84`)."},"5598":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-18","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#key-files","content":"File"},"5599":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-19","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#key-files","content":"Lines"},"5600":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-20","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#key-files","content":"What is there"},"5601":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-21","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#key-files","content":"`…/src/crc32c.js`"},"5602":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-22","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#key-files","content":"`25-39`"},"5603":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-23","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#key-files","content":"The reflected polynomial and the table building logic"},"5604":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-24","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#key-files","content":"`…/storage/SegmentWriter.kt`"},"5605":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-25","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#key-files","content":"`93-96`"},"5606":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-26","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#key-files","content":"The Java-based CRC32C implementation used for checksumming"},"5607":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-27","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#key-files","content":"`…/src/crc32c.js`"},"5608":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-28","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#key-files","content":"`52-57`"},"5609":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-29","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#key-files","content":"The JavaScript implementation of the `crc32c` function"},"5610":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-30","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"The `crc32c` function in JavaScript requires a `>>> 0` at the end because bitwise operators produce signed 32-bit results, which would otherwise cause the sum to be negative half the time (`crc32c.js:17-19`)."},"5611":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-31","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"In the .NET client, the `Crc32C` implementation is provided via forty lines of code in `Crc32C.cs` rather than a NuGet package to avoid making verification an optional dependency (`README.md:94-96`)."},"5612":{"id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation-32","page_id":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients/crc-checksum-implementation#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"A `Producer` in .NET returns `null` for `ProduceAsync` when using `AckPolicy.None`, as no offset exists until the batch reaches the broker (`README.md:51-52`)."},"5613":{"id":"/wiki/clients","page_id":"/wiki/clients","type":"page","content":"clients","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","clients"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients"},"5614":{"id":"/wiki/clients-0","page_id":"/wiki/clients","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"What this module is responsible for"},"5615":{"id":"/wiki/clients-1","page_id":"/wiki/clients","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients#diagram","content":"D