d-33","page_id":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and#key-files","content":"Explanation of round-robin behavior."},"6275":{"id":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and-34","page_id":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and#key-files","content":"`…/java/README.md`"},"6276":{"id":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and-35","page_id":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and#key-files","content":"`54-57`"},"6277":{"id":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and-36","page_id":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and#key-files","content":"Details on `Producer` ownership of `Connection`."},"6278":{"id":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and-37","page_id":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**`partitionFor(null)`** advances a counter even when just querying; if you call it to \"peek\" at a partition and then call it again to send, you will skip a partition (`README.md:204-207`)."},"6279":{"id":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and-38","page_id":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**`AckPolicy.NONE`** returns `null` in Python, which can be interpreted as a lack of response rather than an empty response, as no offset exists until the broker processes the write (`connection.py:109-111`)."},"6280":{"id":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and-39","page_id":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-python/the-producer-and#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**`TopicHandle`** partitions are determined by asking the broker via metadata rather than being passed as a fixed count, preventing mismatches between client configuration and broker state (`Publishing.kt:14-17`)."},"6281":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","type":"page","content":"BrokerError and ProtocolError","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","clients/node"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror"},"6282":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-0","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"What this module is responsible for"},"6283":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-1","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"6284":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-2","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#brokererror","content":"BrokerError"},"6285":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-3","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#protocolerror","content":"ProtocolError"},"6286":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-4","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#corruptrecorderror","content":"CorruptRecordError"},"6287":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-5","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#recordexceedsmaxbyteserror","content":"RecordExceedsMaxBytesError"},"6288":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-6","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#errorcode","content":"ErrorCode"},"6289":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-7","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#key-files","content":"Key files"},"6290":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-8","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#behaviour-that-does-not-surprise","content":"Behaviour that does not surprise"},"6291":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-9","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `ef58254ca7be`, 2026-08-16, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"6292":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-10","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"This module provides the error hierarchy and protocol-level error definitions for the `booblik` client. It distinguishes between failures that occur during the transport of bytes and failures that occur when the broker logic rejects a validly framed request."},"6293":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-11","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#brokererror","content":"The mechanics of handling refusals from the broker where the connection remains usable. A `BrokerError` occurs when the framing is intact and the broker understands the request, but declines it based on business logic (e.g., an invalid offset or topic) `errors.js:25-32`. Because the framing is intact, the connection stays usable for subsequent requests `errors.js:21-24`. The `ErrorCode` returned by the broker is mapped to a human-readable name via `codeName` `errors.js:14-16`."},"6294":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-12","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#protocolerror","content":"Handling of transport-level failures and framing issues. A `ProtocolError` is raised when the bytes on the connection do not make sense, such as a bad length prefix, a short response, or a lost socket `errors.js:35-40`. Unlike `BrokerError`, these issues often imply that the stream is no longer synchronized, potentially requiring a connection reset."},"6295":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-13","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#corruptrecorderror","content":"The role of CRC-32C checksums in protecting the disk and the client's responsibility in verification. The client is the only party that can detect corruption because the broker uses zero-copy paths that do not touch the data bytes `protocol-wire.md:154-156`. If a client skips checksum verification, it effectively disables the project's primary defense against log corruption `errors.js:48-49`. The error includes the `offset`, `stored` checksum, and `computed` checksum to facilitate debugging `errors.js:53-57`."},"6296":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-14","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#recordexceedsmaxbyteserror","content":"The distinction between broker-side record limits and client-side reading limits. This error is thrown when a record is larger than the client's own `maxBytes` limit, meaning the record can never be read in its entirety `errors.js:67-71`. This is distinct from `Code.RECORD_TOO_LARGE`, which refers to the broker's refusal to store a record that is too big for a segment `errors.js:73-75`."},"6297":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-15","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#errorcode","content":"Enumeration of wire-level refusal codes."},"6298":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-16","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#errorcode","content":"Code"},"6299":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-17","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#errorcode","content":"Name"},"6300":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-18","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#errorcode","content":"Description"},"6301":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-19","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#errorcode","content":"0"},"6302":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-20","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#errorcode","content":"`NONE`"},"6303":{"id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror-21","page_id":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-node/brokererror-and-protocolerror#erro