","url":"/wiki/dev-common/atomic-offset-persistence#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"The `SustainedWriteProbe` is designed to intentionally saturate the OS writeback to observe the performance degradation of the `MAPPED` mode `SustainedWriteProbe.kt:32-33`."},"6831":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","type":"page","content":"FileOffsetStore","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","dev/common"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore"},"6832":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-0","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"What this module is responsible for"},"6833":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-1","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"6834":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-2","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#fileoffsetstore","content":"FileOffsetStore"},"6835":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-3","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#atomic-move-via-temporary-files","content":"Atomic move via temporary files"},"6836":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-4","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#at-least-once-checkpointing","content":"At-least-once checkpointing"},"6837":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-5","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#file-based-position-recovery","content":"File-based position recovery"},"6838":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-6","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#key-files","content":"Key files"},"6839":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-7","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"Behaviour that surprises"},"6840":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-8","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-16, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"6841":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-9","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"The `FileOffsetStore` provides a simple implementation of the `OffsetStore` interface, designed for consumers that need to persist their position in a log on a local volume. It ensures that a consumer's position outlives the process by storing the `Offset` in a file, allowing for recovery after a restart `FileOffsetStore.kt:27-29`."},"6842":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-10","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#fileoffsetstore","content":"The `FileOffsetStore` is a concrete implementation of `OffsetStore` that uses the local file system to track progress. It maps a combination of `TopicName` and `PartitionId` to a specific file path within a configured directory `FileOffsetStore.kt:61-64`."},"6843":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-11","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#atomic-move-via-temporary-files","content":"To prevent data corruption, the `save` operation does not overwrite the existing offset file directly. Instead, it writes the new offset to a sibling file with a `.tmp` extension and then performs an atomic move using `StandardCopyOption.ATOMIC_MOVE` `FileOffsetStore.kt:55-57`. This ensures that a partially written file (e.g., a truncated `\"12\"` becoming `\"1\"`) does not result in a valid but incorrect offset that could cause silent record replays `FileOffsetStore.kt:23-25`."},"6844":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-12","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#at-least-once-checkpointing","content":"The system guarantees at-least-once delivery by performing `checkpointing` only **after** the collector has successfully handled a batch of records `README.md:35-36`. If a failure occurs between the processing of the batch and the call to `save`, the consumer will restart from the previous offset and replay the batch `README.md:36`."},"6845":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-13","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#file-based-position-recovery","content":"When a consumer restarts, it uses the `load` function to retrieve the last known `Offset` from the file system `FileOffsetStore.kt:34-46`. Because the broker does not store consumer positions, the responsibility for maintaining this state lies entirely with the client/consumer `feature-subscribe-and-publish.md:30-31`."},"6846":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-14","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#key-files","content":"File"},"6847":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-15","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#key-files","content":"Lines"},"6848":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-16","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#key-files","content":"What is there"},"6849":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-17","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#key-files","content":"`…/common/FileOffsetStore.kt`"},"6850":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-18","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#key-files","content":"`27-64`"},"6851":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-19","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#key-files","content":"Implementation of `FileOffsetStore` including `load`, `save`, and file path resolution."},"6852":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-20","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"The `save` method uses a temporary file and `StandardCopyOption.ATOMIC_MOVE` to ensure that a position saved halfway through a write does not result in a truncated offset `FileOffsetStore.kt:55-57`."},"6853":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-21","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"`checkpointing` is designed for at-least-once semantics; saving the offset before handling the batch would result in at-most-once delivery, potentially skipping records `README.md:35-36`."},"6854":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore-22","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common/fileoffsetstore#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"The `load` function returns `null` if the offset file does not exist, which is treated as a valid starting point for a new consumer `FileOffsetStore.kt:40`."},"6855":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common","type":"page","content":"dev/common","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","dev/common"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-common"},"6856":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common-0","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-common#diagram"