Store`"},"6879":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common-23","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common#public-api","content":"`FileOffsetStore.kt:27`"},"6880":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common-24","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common#public-api","content":"Provides a filesystem-based implementation of the `OffsetStore` interface."},"6881":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common-25","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"`save` uses a temporary file and an atomic move (`FileOffsetStore.kt:55-57`) to ensure that a partially written offset does not corrupt the state."},"6882":{"id":"/wiki/dev-common-26","page_id":"/wiki/dev-common","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-common#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"`load` returns `null` if the offset file does not exist on the disk (`FileOffsetStore.kt:40`)."},"6883":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","type":"page","content":"Connection and Topic Management","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","clients/java"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic"},"6884":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-0","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"6885":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-1","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#booblikconnection-and-the-pipelined-request-queue","content":"BooblikConnection and the Pipelined Request Queue"},"6886":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-2","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#session-and-the-protocol-loop","content":"Session and the Protocol Loop"},"6887":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-3","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#metadatarequest-and-topic-discovery","content":"MetadataRequest and Topic Discovery"},"6888":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-4","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#connectionclosedexception-and-failure-propagation","content":"ConnectionClosedException and Failure Propagation"},"6889":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-5","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#the-producer-connection-ownership-model","content":"The Producer-Connection Ownership Model"},"6890":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-6","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#key-files","content":"Key files"},"6891":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-7","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"Behaviour that surprising"},"6892":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-8","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `ef58254ca7be`, 2026-08-16, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"6893":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-9","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#booblikconnection-and-the-pipelined-request-queue","content":"The `BooblikConnection` implements a pipelined architecture where many requests can be in flight simultaneously. To achieve this, it uses a `ConcurrentLinkedQueue` of `Pending` objects to track requests that have been sent but not yet answered `BooblikConnection.kt:60`. Because the broker is guaranteed to answer requests in the order they were received, the client uses a FIFO queue to match incoming responses back to their original callers via a `correlationId` `BooblikConnection.kt:34-37`. To prevent interleaved writes on the socket, a single writer coroutine drains the outbound channel, ensuring that the wire order matches the request order `BooblikConnection.kt:74-83`."},"6894":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-10","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#session-and-the-protocol-loop","content":"The `Session` class runs the primary protocol loop, which continuously reads frames from a connection and dispatches them for handling `Session.kt:50`. The lifecycle begins with `readFrame`, which validates the length prefix to prevent large allocation attacks `Session.kt:68-70`. Once a frame is read, `handle` uses a `when` expression to decode the request; if `RequestDecoder.decode` returns a `DecodeResult.Failed`, the session immediately responds with an error to the client `Session.kt:81-89`."},"6895":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-11","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#metadatarequest-and-topic-discovery","content":"`MetadataRequest` is used to discover the state of topics and partitions. When a request is processed, the broker checks if the requested topics exist in its registry `Session.kt:122`. If a named topic is not found, the broker does not simply omit it from the response; instead, it fails the entire request with an `UNKNOWN_TOPIC_OR_PARTITION` error to prevent clients from waiting indefinitely for a topic that does not exist `Session.kt:127-130`."},"6896":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-12","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#connectionclosedexception-and-failure-propagation","content":"When a network error or a fatal protocol error occurs, the `fail(cause: Throwable)` function is invoked to clean up the connection `BooblikConnection.kt:161-163`. This function performs several critical tasks:"},"6897":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-13","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#connectionclosedexception-and-failure-propagation","content":"It marks the connection as failed."},"6898":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-14","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#connectionclosedexception-and-failure-propagation","content":"It closes the outbound channel."},"6899":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-15","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#connectionclosedexception-and-failure-propagation","content":"It iterates through all `pending` requests in the queue and completes them exceptionally with a `ConnectionClosedException` `BooblikConnection.kt:166-167`."},"6900":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-16","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#the-producer-connection-ownership-model","content":"To maintain the integrity of the pipelined protocol, a `Producer` must own its `Connection`. This is because a `Producer` manages its own pending records and is the only writer to its specific socket `README.md:49-53`. If a user attempts to use the same `Connection` directly while a `Producer` is active, the responses may be mismatched because the broker's responses are matched strictly by order `README.md:54-56`."},"6901":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-17","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#key-files","content":"File"},"6902":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-18","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#key-files","content":"Lines"},"6903":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-19","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#key-files","content":"What is there"},"6904":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-20","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#key-files","content":"`…/client/BooblikConnection.kt`"},"6905":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-21","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#key-files","content":"`58-61`"},"6906":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-22","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#key-files","content":"Outbound channel and pending request queue"},"6907":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-23","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#key-files","content":"`…/net/Session.kt`"},"6908":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-24","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#key-files","content":"`47-55`"},"6909":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-25","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#key-files","content":"The main protocol loop and frame reading"},"6910":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-26","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#key-files","content":"`…/client/BooblikConnection.kt`"},"6911":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-27","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#key-files","content":"`184-240`"},"6912":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-28","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#key-files","content":"The `Pending` sealed class hierarchy for matching responses"},"6913":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-29","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"A `MetadataRequest` that names a non-existent topic will result in an error for the entire request rather than just omitting the missing topic `Session.kt:127-130`."},"6914":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-30","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"If a `Connection` fails, all currently waiting `Pending` requests are immediately failed with a `ConnectionClosedException` `BooblikConnection.kt:167`."},"6915":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic-31","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java/connection-and-topic#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"The `Session` will continue to keep a connection open even if a `DecodeResult.Failed` occurs, as long as the framing remains intact `Session.kt:78-79`."},"6916":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","type":"page","content":"clients/java","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","clients/java"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java"},"6917":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-0","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"What this module is responsible for"},"6918":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-1","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"6919":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-2","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java#connection-and-topic-management","content":"Connection and Topic Management"},"6920":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-3","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"Producer Configuration and Batching"},"6921":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-4","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java#produceresult-and-ackpolicy","content":"ProduceResult and AckPolicy"},"6922":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-5","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java#partitioninfo-and-partitioning","content":"PartitionInfo and Partitioning"},"6923":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-6","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java#consumer-iteration-and-position-management","content":"Consumer Iteration and Position Management"},"6924":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-7","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java#recordexceedsmaxbytesexception","content":"RecordExceedsMaxBytesException"},"6925":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-8","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java#key-files","content":"Key files"},"6926":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-9","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/clients-java#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"Behaviour that surprise"},"6927":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-10","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `ef58254ca7be`, 2026-08-16, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"6928":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-11","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"Documentation for the booblik Java client module."},"6929":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-12","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#connection-and-topic-management","content":"The lifecycle of a `Connection` is managed via a try-with-resources block, as seen in the usage examples in `README.md:9-12`. Topics are accessed through the connection via the `topic(String)` method, which retrieves partition information directly from the broker as described in `README.md:10`."},"6930":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-13","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#connection-and-topic-management","content":"More: Connection and Topic Management"},"6931":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-14","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"Performance is heavily dependent on the accumulator, where batching significantly increases throughput compared to sending single records (`README.md:36-37`). Users can tune the accumulator using `ProducerConfig`, which is defined in `ProducerConfig.java:4`."},"6932":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-15","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"The `ProducerConfig` parameters are:"},"6933":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-16","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"Parameter"},"6934":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-17","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"Type"},"6935":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-18","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"Description"},"6936":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-19","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"`maxBatchSize`"},"6937":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-20","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"`int`"},"6938":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-21","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"The maximum size of a batch"},"6939":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-22","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"`lingerMillis`"},"6940":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-23","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"`long`"},"6941":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-24","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"Time to wait before sending a batch"},"6942":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-25","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"`ack`"},"6943":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-26","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"`AckPolicy`"},"6944":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-27","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"The acknowledgement policy"},"6945":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-28","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"The default configuration is provided by `ProducerConfig.defaults()` in `ProducerConfig.java:15`."},"6946":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-29","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#producer-configuration-and-batching","content":"More: Producer Configuration and Batching"},"6947":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-30","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#produceresult-and-ackpolicy","content":"A produce operation returns a `ProduceResult`, which contains the `baseOffset` and `logEndOffset` of the written batch (`ProduceResult.java:4`)."},"6948":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-31","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#produceresult-and-ackpolicy","content":"The `AckPolicy` determines the acknowledgement behavior:"},"6949":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-32","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#produceresult-and-ackpolicy","content":"Mode"},"6950":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-33","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#produceresult-and-ackpolicy","content":"Behavior"},"6951":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-34","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#produceresult-and-ackpolicy","content":"`WRITTEN`"},"6952":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-35","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#produceresult-and-ackpolicy","content":"Standard acknowledgement"},"6953":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-36","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#produceresult-and-ackpolicy","content":"`NONE`"},"6954":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-37","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#produceresult-and-ackpolicy","content":"Returns `null` or `Producer.OFFSET_UNKNOWN`; broker may drop records silently (`README.md:59-64`)"},"6955":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-38","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#partitioninfo-and-partitioning","content":"Metadata for a partition is encapsulated in the `PartitionInfo` record, which includes the `partition` index, the `logStartOffset` (the start of the live log after retention), and the `highWatermark` (`PartitionInfo.java:7-9`)."},"6956":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-39","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#partitioninfo-and-partitioning","content":"Partitioning logic is influenced by the key; while `topic.send` uses a key, the client's internal logic ensures that the key itself is not sent to the broker, but rather the partition index is determined by the key (`README.md:65-67`)."},"6957":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-40","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#consumer-iteration-and-position-management","content":"The `Consumer` implements `Iterable<byte[]>`, allowing for a standard for-each loop (`README.md:90-92`). The loop is blocking: `hasNext()` will block until data is available or the socket times out (`README.md:101`)."},"6958":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-41","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#consumer-iteration-and-position-management","content":"To ensure \"at-least-once\" delivery, the caller must manually track the `position()` of the consumer and persist it *after* the records are processed (`README.md:93-94`)."},"6959":{"id":"/wiki/clients-java-42","page_id":"/wiki/clients-java","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/clients-java#recordexceedsmaxbytesexception","content":"If a record is larger than the client's configured `maxBytes` limit, a `RecordExceedsMaxBytesException` is thrown (`README.md:115-116`). This is a terminal error that cannot be resolved by retrying, as the record will never fit in the buffer (`RecordExceedsMaxBytesException.java:10-13`)."},"6960":