ontent":"The `build` function containing the replay and follow logic"},"7233":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection-26","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection#key-files","content":"`…/projection/Main.kt`"},"7234":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection-27","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection#key-files","content":"`145-173`"},"7235":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection-28","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection#key-files","content":"The `Progress` class for tracking internal metrics"},"7236":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection-29","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection#key-files","content":"`…/projection/View.kt`"},"7237":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection-30","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection#key-files","content":"`9-22`"},"7238":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection-31","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection#key-files","content":"Data classes for `Event` and `UserView`"},"7239":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection-32","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection#key-files","content":"`…/projection/View.kt`"},"7240":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection-33","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection#key-files","content":"`39-77`"},"7241":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection-34","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection#key-files","content":"The `Projection` class implementing the state machine"},"7242":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection-35","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection#behaviour-that-should-surprise","content":"The `Projection` class does not persist its state to disk; instead, it relies on the fact that it can rebuild the entire state by replaying the log from the beginning `View.kt:25-32`."},"7243":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection-36","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection#behaviour-that-should-surprise","content":"If a record cannot be decoded, the `apply` function increments the `skipped` counter but continues processing the log rather than stopping `View.kt:49-53`."},"7244":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection-37","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection#behaviour-that-should-surprise","content":"The `follow` stage uses a separate `CoroutineScope` for each partition to allow concurrent consumption of partition streams `Main.kt:111-130`."},"7245":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","type":"page","content":"Projection","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","dev/projection"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection"},"7246":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-0","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"7247":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-1","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#the-projection-lifecycle","content":"The Projection lifecycle"},"7248":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-2","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#the-projection-state-machine","content":"The Projection state machine"},"7249":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-3","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#recovery-after-a-crash","content":"Recovery after a crash"},"7250":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-4","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#verification-of-the-read-model","content":"Verification of the read model"},"7251":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-5","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#key-files","content":"Key files"},"7252":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-6","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"Behaviour that surprising"},"7253":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-7","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-15, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"7254":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-8","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","content":"Documentation for the Projection module, focusing on the read model implementation and its verification."},"7255":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-9","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#the-projection-lifecycle","content":"The lifecycle of a projection is split into two distinct phases to ensure the view is both complete and current. It begins with a `replay()` phase that reads from the `Earliest` position to build the initial state, and transitions to a `follow()` phase once the history has been exhausted `Main.kt:98-110`."},"7256":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-10","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#the-projection-state-machine","content":"The state is managed within the `Projection` class, where the `apply` function performs a functional fold over the incoming stream `View.kt:44-67`. The `UserView` is updated by merging new actions into the existing map and incrementing event counts. Crucially, the correctness of `lastAction` depends on the fact that all events for a single user are routed to the same partition, ensuring they arrive in order `View.kt:34-37`."},"7257":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-11","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#recovery-after-a-crash","content":"The design follows a \"persist neither\" philosophy to avoid silent corruption. Because the `Projection` does not persist its position to a volume, a restart forces a complete rebuild from the beginning of the log `View.kt:27-32`. This ensures that the view is always a complete reflection of the log, rather than a potentially truncated view that resumes from a stale offset `README.md:140-144`."},"7258":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-12","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#verification-of-the-read-model","content":"The verification suite, primarily implemented in `dev/check-projection.sh`, asserts several invariants:"},"7259":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-13","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#verification-of-the-read-model","content":"**Rebuild Completeness**: After a restart, the `applied` count must be at least as large as the count before the restart `check.py:204-207`."},"7260":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-14","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#verification-of-the-read-model","content":"**View Consistency**: The sum of all `events` across all users must exactly match the total number of `applied` events `check.py:181-184`."},"7261":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-15","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#verification-of-the-read-model","content":"**User Integrity**: For any specific user, the sum of counts in the `actions` map must equal the total `events` count for that user `check.py:224-226`."},"7262":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-16","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#key-files","content":"File"},"7263":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-17","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#key-files","content":"Lines"},"7264":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-18","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#key-files","content":"What is there"},"7265":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-19","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#key-files","content":"`…/projection/View.kt`"},"7266":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-20","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#key-files","content":"`10-22`"},"7267":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-21","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#key-files","content":"`Event` and `UserView` data classes"},"7268":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-22","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#key-files","content":"`…/projection/View.kt`"},"7269":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-23","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#key-files","content":"`39-77`"},"7270":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-24","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#key-files","content":"`Projection` class containing the state and `apply` logic"},"7271":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection-25","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/projection#key-files","content":"`…/pr