i/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle#key-files","content":"Logic for asserting that the rebuilt view matches the input."},"7313":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle-29","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle#key-files","content":"`…/net/SubscriptionTest.kt`"},"7314":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle-30","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle#key-files","content":"`143-172`"},"7315":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle-31","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle#key-files","content":"Test case for at-least-once semantics during failures."},"7316":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle-32","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**Silent Corruption Risk**: If a service were to persist its position without its state, it would result in a silent corruption rather than an optimization `README.md:41-42`."},"7317":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle-33","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**Replay Completion**: The `replayComplete` flag is only set once the `replay` flow from the subscriber actually completes `Main.kt:105`."},"7318":{"id":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle-34","page_id":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-projection/the-build-lifecycle#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**Non-monotonicity in `follow`**: While `follow` ensures the view stays current, the `follow` phase does not end, unlike `replay` which terminates once the high watermark is reached `Main.kt:35`."},"7319":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","type":"page","content":"dev/publisher","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","dev/publisher"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher"},"7320":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-0","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"7321":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-1","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#publisherconfig","content":"PublisherConfig"},"7322":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-2","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#openconnection","content":"openConnection"},"7323":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-3","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#publishforever","content":"publishForever"},"7324":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-4","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#publishtasks","content":"publishTasks"},"7325":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-5","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#stats","content":"Stats"},"7326":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-6","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#embeddedserver","content":"embeddedServer"},"7327":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-7","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#key-files","content":"Key files"},"7328":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-8","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"Behaviour that Surprises"},"7329":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-9","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `ef58254ca7be`, 2026-08-16, sources: 2. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"7330":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-10","page_id":"/wiki/