terface providing health checks and JSON-serialized statistics via Ktor, initialized in `Main.kt:58-64`."},"7363":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-43","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#key-files","content":"File"},"7364":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-44","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#key-files","content":"Lines"},"7365":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-45","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#key-files","content":"What is there"},"7366":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-46","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#key-files","content":"`…/publisher/build.gradle.kts`"},"7367":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-47","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#key-files","content":"`1-7`"},"7368":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-48","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#key-files","content":"Dependencies for the client, Ktor server, and serialization."},"7369":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-49","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#key-files","content":"`…/publisher/Main.kt`"},"7370":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-50","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#key-files","content":"`35-66`"},"7371":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-51","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#key-files","content":"The `main` entry point that orchestrates the connection, producers, and the server."},"7372":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-52","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"The `publishForever` function uses `topic.partitionFor(key)` to determine the partition before sending, which is a stable pure function of the key, unlike round-robin partitioners that might advance a counter (`Main.kt:97-101`)."},"7373":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-53","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"The `publishTasks` function explicitly uses `PartitionId(0)` to ensure all tasks go into a single partition, preventing the splitting that would occur if it used a keyed partitioner (`Main.kt:120-122`)."},"7374":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher-54","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"The `openConnection` function uses an infinite `while(true)` loop to retry connection attempts until the broker is reachable, preventing startup race conditions (`Main.kt:78-84`)."},"7375":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","type":"page","content":"openConnection","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","dev/publisher"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection"},"7376":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-0","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"What this module is responsible for"},"7377":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-1","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"7378":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-2","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#the-openconnection-retry-loop","content":"The `openConnection` retry loop"},"7379":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-3","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#broker-availability-and-startup-race-conditions","content":"Broker availability and startup race conditions"},"7380":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-4","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#booblikconnection-instantiation","content":"BooblikConnection instantiation"},"7381":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-5","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#key-files","content":"Key files"},"7382":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-6","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"Behaviour that surprises"},"7383":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-7","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-15, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"7384":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-8","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"The `dev/publisher` module is responsible for simulating event streams and task queues to test the Booblik broker. Within this module, the `openConnection` mechanism ensures that the publisher can gracefully handle the lifecycle of the broker, specifically managing the transition from a container starting up to a state where the network socket is actually accepting connections."},"7385":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-9","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#the-openconnection-retry-loop","content":"The `openConnection` function implements a blocking retry mechanism to establish a `BooblikConnection`. It first resolves the broker's location into an `InetSocketAddress` using the host and port provided in the `PublisherConfig` (`Main.kt:77`). If the connection attempt fails, the function catches the exception, prints a retry message including the failure reason, and waits for 1000 milliseconds before attempting to connect again (`Main.kt:82-83`)."},"7386":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-10","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#broker-availability-and-startup-race-conditions","content":"The retry loop is a defensive measure against startup race conditions in containerized environments. While `docker-compose.yml:44-46` uses `condition: service_healthy` to ensure the publisher only starts after the broker's health check passes, the code includes the loop because \"should never\" and \"does not\" are different claims (`Main.kt:72-74`). This prevents the publisher from crashing if the broker's process is running but the network stack is not yet ready to accept connections."},"7387":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-11","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#booblikconnection-instantiation","content":"Once a connection is successfully established, `openConnection` returns a new `BooblikConnection` instance (`Main.kt:80`). Crucially, this connection is initialized with its own `CoroutineScope` configured with a `SupervisorJob` (`Main.kt:80`). This ensures that failures in child coroutines within the connection do not automatically cancel the entire scope, allowing for more robust error handling during the publisher's execution."},"7388":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-12","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#key-files","content":"File"},"7389":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-13","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#key-files","content":"Lines"},"7390":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-14","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#key-files","content":"What is there"},"7391":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-15","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#key-files","content":"`…/publisher/Main.kt`"},"7392":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-16","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#key-files","content":"`76-86`"},"7393":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-17","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#key-files","content":"The `openConnection` implementation containing the retry logic and `InetSocketAddress` setup."},"7394":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-18","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#key-files","content":"`dev/docker-compose.yml`"},"7395":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-19","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#key-files","content":"`44-46`"},"7396":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-20","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#key-files","content":"The `depends_on` configuration using `service_healthy` to coordinate service startup."},"7397":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-21","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**Scope Isolation**: The `BooblikConnection` created in `openConnection` is given a new `CoroutineScope` with a `SupervisorJob` rather than using the caller's scope, which prevents a connection failure from propagating up and killing the entire publisher application (`Main.kt:80`)."},"7398":{"id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection-22","page_id":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-publisher/openconnection#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**The \"Should Never\" Clause**: Despite the orchestration provided by Docker Compose, the `openConnection` function explicitly includes a `while(true)` loop to handle the edge case where a broker is \"not answering yet\" (`Main.kt:78-82`)."},"7399":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","type":"page","content":"booblikToKafka","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","dev/relay"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka"},"7400":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-0","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"What this module is responsible for"},"7401":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-1","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"7402":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-2","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#the-boobliktokafka-lifecycle","content":"The `booblikToKafka` lifecycle"},"7403":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-3","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#the-fileoffsetstore-mechanism","content":"The `FileOffsetStore` mechanism"},"7404":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-4","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#at-least-once-delivery-and-kafkaflush","content":"At-least-once delivery and `kafka.flush`"},"7405":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-5","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#the-mirrored-topic-and-partition-mapping","content":"The `mirrored` topic and partition mapping"},"7406":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-6","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#key-files","content":"Key files"},"7407":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-7","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"Behaviour that surprises"},"7408":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-8","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-15, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"7409":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-9","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"The `booblikToKafka` relay acts as a bridge that consumes data from a booblik topic and produces it into a Kafka topic. Unlike the reverse direction, this relay is responsible for managing its own state because the booblik broker does not track consumer positions."},"7410":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-10","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#the-boobliktokafka-lifecycle","content":"The lifecycle begins with the `BooblikSubscriber.follow` method, which initiates a stream from the booblik topic using a position retrieved from the `FileOffsetStore` (`Directions.kt:110-111`). The stream is processed via the `collect` operator, which receives batches of records. The `checkpointing` operator is applied to the flow, ensuring that the `OffsetStore` is updated only after the collector has successfully processed the batch (`Directions.kt:112`)."},"7411":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-11","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#the-fileoffsetstore-mechanism","content":"Since the booblik broker does not remember readers, the relay maintains state using a `FileOffsetStore` on its own volume (`Directions.kt:93`). To ensure position integrity, the `save` method writes the offset to a temporary file and then performs an atomic move using `StandardCopyOption.ATOMIC_MOVE` (`FileOffsetStore.kt:57`). This prevents a partially written or truncated offset from being parsed during a restart (`FileOffsetStore.kt:25`)."},"7412":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-12","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#at-least-once-delivery-and-kafkaflush","content":"The relay guarantees at-least-once delivery through a specific sequence of operations within the `collect` block. First, all records in a batch are sent to Kafka via `kafka.send` (`Directions.kt:117`). Second, `kafka.flush()` is called to ensure all buffered records are actually acknowledged by the Kafka broker (`Directions.kt:119`). Only after the flush is successful does the `checkpointing` mechanism save the `batch.nextOffset` to the `FileOffsetStore` (`Directions.kt:120`)."},"7413":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-13","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#the-mirrored-topic-and-partition-mapping","content":"When moving data from booblik to Kafka, the relay faces a limitation: booblik's wire protocol does not store keys, only the `partitionId` (`README.md:177-179`). Consequently, when the relay calls `kafka.send(ProducerRecord(config.kafkaTopic, record))`, it does not provide a key (`Directions.kt:117`). This means the distribution of records into Kafka partitions is determined by Kafka's default partitioning logic rather than any specific key-based rule chosen by the original producer."},"7414":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-14","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#key-files","content":"File"},"7415":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-15","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#key-files","content":"Lines"},"7416":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-16","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#key-files","content":"What is there"},"7417":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-17","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#key-files","content":"`…/relay/Directions.kt`"},"7418":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-18","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#key-files","content":"`89-124`"},"7419":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-19","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#key-files","content":"The `booblikToKafka` function implementation and its logic."},"7420":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-20","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#key-files","content":"`…/common/FileOffsetStore.kt`"},"7421":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-21","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#key-files","content":"`27-61`"},"7422":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-22","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#key-files","content":"The `FileOffsetStore` class and its atomic file-based persistence logic."},"7423":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-23","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#key-files","content":"`…/relay/Main.kt`"},"7424":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-24","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#key-files","content":"`47-70`"},"7425":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-25","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#key-files","content":"The `main` function containing the reconnection loop and error handling."},"7426":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-26","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**At-least-once duplicates**: Because the `checkpointing` happens after `kafka.flush()`, a crash between these two calls will result in the same batch being re-sent to Kafka upon restart (`Directions.kt:119-120`)."},"7427":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-27","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**Key loss**: While the `TopicHandle.send` in the `kafkaToBooblik` direction uses the Kafka key to pick a booblik partition, the `booblikToKafka` direction loses this key entirely because it is not part of the booblik wire protocol (`README.md:177-180`)."},"7428":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka-28","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/boobliktokafka#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**Silent corruption prevention**: The `FileOffsetStore` uses a `.tmp` file and an atomic move specifically to avoid the \"half-saved\" offset bug where a truncated file could lead to silent data replay (`FileOffsetStore.kt:24-25`)."},"7429":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","type":"page","content":"Directional modes","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","dev/relay"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes"},"7430":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-0","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"7431":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-1","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"Directional Configuration and Environment"},"7432":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-2","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#kafka-to-booblik-consumer-group-and-manual-commit","content":"Kafka to booblik: Consumer Group and Manual Commit"},"7433":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-3","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#booblik-to-kafka-fileoffsetstore-and-checkpointing","content":"booblik to Kafka: FileOffsetStore and Checkpointing"},"7434":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-4","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#the-key-to-partition-mapping","content":"The Key-to-Partition Mapping"},"7435":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-5","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#key-files","content":"Key files"},"7436":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-6","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"Behaviour that surprises"},"7437":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-7","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-15, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"7438":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-8","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"The behavior of the relay is determined by the `Direction` enum, which is parsed from the `RELAY_DIRECTION` environment variable (defaulting to `KAFKA_TO_BOOBLIK`) in `Main.kt:159-163`. The `RelayConfig` class encapsulates all necessary parameters, including bootstrap servers and topic names, which are loaded from the environment in `Main.kt:157-174`."},"7439":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-9","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"Environment Variable"},"7440":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-10","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"`RelayConfig` Property"},"7441":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-11","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"Default Value"},"7442":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-12","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"`RELAY_DIRECTION`"},"7443":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-13","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"`direction`"},"7444":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-14","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"`KAFKA_TO_BOOBLIK`"},"7445":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-15","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"`BOOBLIK_HOST`"},"7446":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-16","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"`brokerHost`"},"7447":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-17","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"`127.0.0.1`"},"7448":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-18","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"`KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP`"},"7449":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-19","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"`kafkaBootstrap`"},"7450":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-20","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"`kafka:9092`"},"7451":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-21","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"`KAFKA_TOPIC`"},"7452":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-22","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"`kafkaTopic`"},"7453":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-23","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#directional-configuration-and-environment","content":"`orders`"},"7454":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-24","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#kafka-to-booblik-consumer-group-and-manual-commit","content":"When operating in the `KAFKA_TO_BOOBLIK` direction, the relay acts as a Kafka consumer. To ensure delivery guarantees, `ENABLE_AUTO_COMMIT_CONFIG` is explicitly set to `false` in `Directions.kt:49`. The process follows a strict lifecycle: it polls records, sends them to booblik via a `Producer`, and only after the booblik acknowledgements are received does it call `consumer.commitSync()` in `Directions.kt:71`. This ensures that the Kafka consumer group position only advances once the data is safely in booblik."},"7455":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-25","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#booblik-to-kafka-fileoffsetstore-and-checkpointing","content":"In the `BOOBLIK_TO_KAFKA` direction, the broker does not track the reader's position. Instead, the relay uses a `FileOffsetStore` to persist the state locally on a volume, as seen in `Directions.kt:93`. The `booblikToKafka` function uses a `checkpointing` operator that saves the offset only after the `collector` has successfully handled the batch, ensuring that the `FileOffsetStore` is updated only after the Kafka producer has finished its work (`Directions.kt:112`)."},"7456":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-26","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#the-key-to-partition-mapping","content":"The relay handles Kafka keys differently depending on the direction. In `kafkaToBooblik`, the Kafka record key is passed to `handle.send(record.value(), key = record.key())` in `Directions.kt:66`, which allows the key to influence partition selection in booblik, preserving per-key ordering. However, because the booblik wire format does not contain a field for the key, the key itself is not stored and is lost for any subsequent round trip (`Main.kt:37-42`)."},"7457":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-27","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#key-files","content":"File"},"7458":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-28","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#key-files","content":"Lines"},"7459":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-29","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#key-files","content":"What is there"},"7460":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-30","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#key-files","content":"`…/relay/Main.kt`"},"7461":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-31","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#key-files","content":"`83-86`"},"7462":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-32","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#key-files","content":"`Direction` enum definition"},"7463":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-33","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#key-files","content":"`…/relay/Main.kt`"},"7464":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-34","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#key-files","content":"`142-153`"},"7465":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-35","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#key-files","content":"`RelayConfig` data class and environment loading"},"7466":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-36","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#key-files","content":"`…/relay/Directions.kt`"},"7467":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-37","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#key-files","content":"`38-77`"},"7468":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-38","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#key-files","content":"`kafkaToBooblik` implementation"},"7469":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-39","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#key-files","content":"`…/relay/Directions.kt`"},"7470":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-40","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#key-files","content":"`89-124`"},"7471":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-41","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#key-files","content":"`booblikToKafka` implementation"},"7472":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-42","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"The `kafkaToBooblik` function uses `withContext(Dispatchers.IO)` to wrap the blocking `consumer.poll` and `consumer.commitSync` calls to avoid blocking the coroutine scope (`Directions.kt:62, 71`)."},"7473":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-43","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"In the `BOOBLIK_TO_KAFKA` direction, the relay uses `kafka.flush()` before calling `stats.observe` to ensure that all buffered records are actually sent to Kafka before the position is updated (`Directions.kt:119`)."},"7474":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes-44","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/directional-modes#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"The `RelayConfig` uses `replace` logic for environment variables, where the `direction` string is transformed by converting it to uppercase and replacing hyphens with underscores (`Main.kt:160-162`)."},"7475":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","type":"page","content":"dev/relay","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","dev/relay"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay"},"7476":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-0","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"7477":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-1","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"Directional modes"},"7478":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-2","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay#boobliktokafka","content":"booblikToKafka"},"7479":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-3","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay#at-least-once-delivery-guarantees","content":"At-least-once delivery guarantees"},"7480":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-4","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relaystats","content":"RelayStats"},"7481":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-5","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relayconfig","content":"RelayConfig"},"7482":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-6","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay#key-files","content":"Key files"},"7483":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-7","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"Behaviour that surprise"},"7484":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-8","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay#more","content":"More"},"7485":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-9","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-15, sources: 3. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"7486":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-10","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"The relay operates in one of two modes defined in `Main.kt:83-86`:"},"7487":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-11","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"Mode"},"7488":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-12","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"Description"},"7489":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-13","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"Position Ownership"},"7490":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-14","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"`KAFKA_TO_BOOBLIK`"},"7491":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-15","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"Moves data from Kafka to booblik"},"7492":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-16","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"Managed by Kafka via Consumer Groups (`Directions.kt:46`)"},"7493":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-17","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"`BOOBLIK_TO_KAFKA`"},"7494":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-18","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"Moves data from booblik to Kafka"},"7495":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-19","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"Managed locally via `FileOffsetStore` (`Directions.kt:93`)"},"7496":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-20","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"More: Directional modes"},"7497":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-21","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#boobliktokafka","content":"This mode consumes data from booblik and produces it to Kafka. Because the booblik broker does not remember reader positions, the relay uses a `FileOffsetStore` to manage state locally on the relay's volume (`Directions.kt:93`). To ensure at-least-once delivery, the producer is configured with `acks=all` (`Directions.kt:102`)."},"7498":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-22","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#boobliktokafka","content":"More: booblikToKafka"},"7499":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-23","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#at-least-once-delivery-guarantees","content":"The relay implements at-least-once delivery by ensuring the position is only updated after the destination has acknowledged the data. In `kafkaToBooblik`, `consumer.commitSync()` is called only after all records in a batch are sent to booblik (`Directions.kt:71`). In `booblikToKafka`, the `checkpointing` mechanism saves the position only after the `kafka.flush()` operation is complete (`Directions.kt:119`)."},"7500":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-24","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relaystats","content":"The monitoring surface is exposed via an HTTP server and provides real-time metrics through the `Stats` class (`Main.kt:88`). The `RelayStats` data class (`Main.kt:129`) includes:"},"7501":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-25","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relaystats","content":"`relayed`: Total count of relayed records."},"7502":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-26","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relaystats","content":"`batches`: Total number of batches processed."},"7503":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-27","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relaystats","content":"`position`: The last observed offset/position."},"7504":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-28","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relaystats","content":"`restarts`: Number of times the relay loop has restarted due to failures."},"7505":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-29","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relaystats","content":"`lastFailure`: The message of the last encountered exception."},"7506":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-30","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relaystats","content":"`lastRecord`: A 120-character sample of the last record."},"7507":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-31","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relayconfig","content":"The relay is configured via environment variables as defined in `Main.kt:142-176`. The following parameters are available:"},"7508":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-32","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relayconfig","content":"Parameter"},"7509":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-33","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relayconfig","content":"Environment Variable"},"7510":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-34","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relayconfig","content":"Default Value"},"7511":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-35","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relayconfig","content":"`name`"},"7512":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-36","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relayconfig","content":"`RELAY_NAME`"},"7513":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-37","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relayconfig","content":"`relay`"},"7514":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-38","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":