,"url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"Description"},"7621":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-13","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"`type`"},"7622":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-14","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"`String`"},"7623":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-15","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"Either `claim` or `done`"},"7624":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-16","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"`worker`"},"7625":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-17","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"`String`"},"7626":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-18","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"The identifier of the worker"},"7627":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-19","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"`task`"},"7628":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-20","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"`Long`"},"7629":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-21","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"The unique ID of the task"},"7630":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-22","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"`at`"},"7631":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-23","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"`Long`"},"7632":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-24","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"The claimant's wall clock timestamp"},"7633":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-25","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"`leaseMillis`"},"7634":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-26","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"`Long`"},"7635":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-27","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"The duration the lease is valid for"},"7636":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-28","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimrecord","content":"Serialization is handled via `kotlinx.serialization`, with `encode` and `decode` methods provided in the companion object (`Claims.kt:28-31`)."},"7637":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-29","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimstate","content":"`ClaimState` is a pure, immutable data structure that represents the current view of the queue by replaying the log. The core logic resides in the `apply` function (`Claims.kt:62-91`), which takes a `ClaimRecord` and the `nextOffset` to produce a new state."},"7638":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-30","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimstate","content":"The state tracks:"},"7639":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-31","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimstate","content":"`consumedUpTo`: The last processed offset in the log."},"7640":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-32","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimstate","content":"`leases`: A map of tasks to their current `Lease` (`Claims.kt:59`)."},"7641":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-33","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimstate","content":"`done`: A set of completed task IDs (`Claims.kt:60`)."},"7642":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-34","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#the-lease-lifecycle","content":"The lifecycle of a task is managed through the sequence of records in the log. A task becomes \"claimable\" when it is not in the `done` set and no active lease exists (`Claims.kt:101-104`)."},"7643":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-35","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#the-lease-lifecycle","content":"**Claiming**: A worker writes a `CLAIM` record. The worker must wait for the log to \"settle\" by reading its own claim back to ensure it actually won the race (`Main.kt:184-193`)."},"7644":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-36","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#the-lease-lifecycle","content":"**Holding**: A task is held if the worker's name and the timestamp `at` match the current lease in the state (`Claims.kt:95-98`)."},"7645":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-37","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#the-lease-lifecycle","content":"**Releasing**: A worker writes a `DONE` record, which removes the task from active leases and adds it to the `done` set (`Claims.kt:67-73`)."},"7646":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-38","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#clock-skew-and-determinism","content":"A critical design requirement is that the verdict is a pure function of the log, ensuring all readers reach the same conclusion even if their local clocks differ. As noted in `Claims.kt:47-51`, the `Lease` is judged by comparing the timestamp written *into the claim itself* against the `at` value of the claim, rather than using the reader's local `now()`. This ensures that skew only affects *when* a worker tries to claim a task, not *who* wins the claim once it is written to the log."},"7647":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-39","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimstatetest","content":"The `ClaimStateTest` class verifies the correctness of the state machine through several property-based scenarios (`ClaimStateTest.kt:22-107`):"},"7648":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-40","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimstatetest","content":"**Race Conditions**: Verifies that the first claim in the log wins and subsequent claims within the lease period are ignored (`ClaimStateTest.kt:45-50`)."},"7649":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-41","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimstatetest","content":"**Lease Expiry**: Ensures a claim written after a previous lease has lapsed successfully takes over the task (`ClaimStateTest.kt:54-59`)."},"7650":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-42","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimstatetest","content":"**Completion**: Confirms that once a `DONE` record is processed, the task is no longer claimable (`ClaimStateTest.kt:64-69`)."},"7651":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-43","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#claimstatetest","content":"**Forward Compatibility**: Asserts that unknown record types only advance the `consumedUpTo` offset without disturbing existing leases (`ClaimStateTest.kt:100-107`)."},"7652":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-44","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#key-files","content":"File"},"7653":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the-45","page_id":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-queue-worker/claimrecord-and-the#key-files","content":"Lines"},"7654":{"id":"/wiki/dev-queue-w