is guaranteed to see the corresponding data in the array (`SparseOffsetIndex.kt:80-82`)."],[3849,"The `CrashRecoveryTest` ensures that the system remains consistent even after a `SIGKILL`. It spawns a `CrashWriter` as a separate subprocess to simulate a hard crash (`CrashRecoveryTest.kt:56`). The core invariant verified is that after reopening the segment, the log must end on a valid record boundary, meaning every reported record is readable and matches its original checksum (`CrashRecoveryTest.kt:106`)."],[3867,"The `CrashWriter` subprocess implementation"],[6546,"The `crc32c` checksum"],[6185,"The `crc32c` checksum mechanism"],[6341,"The `crc32c` function and the Castagnoli polynomial"],[6560,"The `crc32c` function implements the Castagnoli polynomial (`0x1EDC6F41`) using a reflected table implementation `algorithms.py:52-54`. It is explicitly noted that this is not `zlib.crc32` or other common CRC-32 implementations, as they use different polynomials `algorithms.py:50`."],[5610,"The `crc32c` function in JavaScript requires a `>>> 0` at the end because bitwise operators produce signed 32-bit results, which would otherwise cause the sum to be negative half the time (`crc32c.js:17-19`)."],[5506,"The `Crc32C` static utility class"],[3653,"The `create` function will throw an `IllegalStateException` rather than issuing a warning if a volatile filesystem is detected, because a warning is often ignored after the number has already been believed (`MeasurementDir.kt:24-25`)."],[3633,"The `create` Lifecycle"],[7281,"The `decode` function in `View.kt` uses `runCatching` to silently skip unreadable records, incrementing a `skipped` counter instead of crashing the projection `View.kt:48-53`."],[3464,"The `deliver` function handles the actual network transmission and the subsequent response from the broker (`Producer.kt:195-220`). The behavior of the caller depends on the `AckPolicy`:"],[7396,"The `depends_on` configuration using `service_healthy` to coordinate service startup.