o specific partitions. The `Partitioner` class provides the `Fnv1a32` hash function which uses an `unchecked` context to allow arithmetic wrapping `Partitioner.cs:33`. The `PartitionFor` method then folds this hash into the range of available partitions using the modulo operator `Partitioner.cs:54`."],[3198,"Validation is performed during initialization to prevent runtime failures (`BooblikConfig.kt:49-55`)."],[5716,"Validation is performed through two distinct scripts. `gate.sh` is used for local checks, selecting a target that the host can actually execute, such as `linuxX64` or `macosArm64` (`README.md:100-104`). The `conformance-client.sh` script handles the heavy lifting of building the binary if necessary and then executing it against a real broker (`conformance-client.sh:37-38`)."],[7175,"Validation of resumed positions"],[3107,"Validation of SegmentMode and FetchMode"],[6155,"Validation of the FNV-1a hashing algorithm and partition assignment against golden vectors. The tests ensure `MatchesTheGoldenVectors` by comparing results against a known-good implementation `PartitionerTests.cs:20-39`. It specifically validates that `HighBytesAreUnsigned` to prevent errors common in signed-integer ports `PartitionerTests.cs:47-51`."],[6145,"Validation of the low-level transport, including byte-for-byte payload integrity, protocol error handling, and metadata routing. Tests ensure that `ARecordArrivesByteForByte` preserves all byte values including nulls `ConnectionTests.cs:17-31`, and that `ATruncatedResponseIsAProtocolError` correctly identifies malformed frames `ConnectionTests.cs:100-103`. It also validates that `MetadataAndKeyRouting` correctly interacts with the partitioner `ConnectionTests.cs:68-79`."],[6681,"Validation via check.sh"],[4909,"Value"],[5463,"Value"],[5529,"Value"],[5920,"Value"],[6199,"Value"],[4337,"Value classes for `Offset`, `TopicName`, and `PartitionId`."],[7331,"Variable"],[3934,"Verb"],[3990,"Verb"],[4041,"Verb"],[4086,"Verb"],[6475,"Verb"]